window.BAHR_DATA=window.BAHR_DATA||{};window.BAHR_DATA["passages-02"]=[{"id":"q2-23-25","q":"2:23–25","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:23–25 · The Qurʾānic challenge and the gardens of the faithful","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 87–90","cairo":"I:87–90","source_page_first":87,"source_page_last":90,"ar":"وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ فِي رَيْبٍ مِمَّا نَزَّلْنا عَلى عَبْدِنا فَأْتُوا بِسُورَةٍ مِنْ مِثْلِهِ وَادْعُوا شُهَداءَكُمْ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (23) فَإِنْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوا وَلَنْ تَفْعَلُوا فَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِي وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجارَةُ أُعِدَّتْ لِلْكافِرِينَ (24) وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ أَنَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ كُلَّما رُزِقُوا مِنْها مِنْ ثَمَرَةٍ رِزْقاً قالُوا هذَا الَّذِي رُزِقْنا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَأُتُوا بِهِ مُتَشابِهاً وَلَهُمْ فِيها أَزْواجٌ مُطَهَّرَةٌ وَهُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (25)\nفإن قلت: الريب في القرآن قد وقع من الكفار قطعاً، فكيف عبّر بإن الدالة على الشك والتردد؟\nقلت: (إن) جازمة للفظ الشرط أو محله، موضوعة للشك في الشرط. و «إذا» لا تجزم في اللفظ، وتدل على الجزم في المعنى، وفي ذلك يقول القائل:\nأنا إنْ شَككتُ وجدْتُموني جَازِماً ... وإذا جَزمتُ فإنني لَمْ أجزمِ\nفإن قلت: الريب في القرآن قد وقع من الكفار قطعاً، فكيف عبر بإن الدالة على الشك والتردد؟ قلت: لما كان ريبهم واقعاً في غير محله- إذ لو تأملوا أدنى تأمل لزال ريبهم لوضوح الأمر وسطوع البرهان- كان ريبهم كأنه مشكوك فيه ومتردد في وقوعه، و (الشهداء) جمع شهيد بمعنى الحاضر، أو القائم بالشهادة، أو الناصر، أُطْلِقَ على الأصنام لأنهم يزعمون أنها تشهد لهم، ومعنى (دون) : أدنى مكان من الشيء، ثم استعير للرُّتَب فقيل: زيد دون عمرو أي: في الشرف، ثم اتسع فيه فاستعير لكل تجاوزِ حدّ إلى حد، وتخطّي أمرٍ إلى آخر.\nيقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ يا معشر الكفار فِي شك مِمَّا نَزَّلْنا عَلى محمد عَبْدِنا ورسولنا المختار لِسِرّ وحينا، فَأْتُوا بِسُورَةٍ مِنْ جنسه في البلاغة والفصاحة، مشتملة على علوم وأسرار ومغيبات كما اشتمل عليه كتابي، وَادْعُوا من استطعتم ممن تنتصرون به على ذلك الإتيان، مِن آلهتكم التي تزعمون أنها تشهد لكم يوم القيامة، أو من حضركم من البلغاء والفصحاء ممن تنتصرون به مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ في أنها تنفعكم. فَإِنْ لَمْ تقدروا أن تَفْعَلُوا ذلك وَلَنْ تقدروا ابداً فأسلموا وأقرُّوا بالحق، فَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِي وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجارَةُ أي: حجارة الكبريت، فَهُمَا حطبُها ووقودها أُعِدَّتْ لِلْكافِرِينَ.\nوَبَشِّرِ يا محمد ويا مَن يصلح منه التبشير الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بالله ورسولِه، وَعَمِلُوا ما كلفوا به من الأعمال الصَّالِحاتِ أَنَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ أي: من تحت قصورها، وهي أنهار من ماء، وأنهار من عسل، وأنهار من لبن، وأنهار من خمر لذة للشاربين. كُلَّما رُزِقُوا مِنْها مِنْ ثَمَرَةٍ رِزْقاً أي: صنفاً، قالُوا هذَا الَّذِي رُزِقْنا مِنْ قَبْلُ في دار الدنيا، فإن الطباع تميل إلى المألوف، فالصفة متفقة والطعم مختلف. أو في الجنة، قيل: هذا لما روى عنه صلى الله عليه وسلّم أنه قال: «والذي نفسُ محمدٍ بيدِه إنَّ الرجلَ مِنْ أهلِ الجنةِ لَيتَناولُ الثمرة لِيأكلهَا فما هي واصِلةٌ إلى جَوفِه حتى يبدل الله تعالى مكانها مِثلَها» ، فلعلهم إذا رأوها على الهيئة الأولى قالوا\nذلك، لفرط استغرابهم، وتبجحهم بما وجدوا من التفاوت العظيم في اللذة والتشابه البليغ في الصورة، وَلَهُمْ فِيها أَزْواجٌ أي: حور مُطَهَّرَةٌ من الحيض، وسائر الأدناس، ومن الأخلاق المذمومة، والشيم الذميمة، وَهُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ فإن النعيم إذا كان يعقُبه الفناء تنغّص على صاحبه، كما قال الشاعر:\nلا خيرَ في العيش مادامت مُنغَّصَةً ... لَذاتُه بادِّكارِ الموتِ والهَرَمِ\nالإشارة: وإن كنتم يا معشر العوام في شك مما خصصنا به ولينا من الأنوار، وما أنزلنا على قلبه من المعارف والأسرار، وما ظهر عليه من البهجة والأنوار، وما اهتدى على يديه من الصالحين والأبرار، فأتوا أنتم بشئ من ذلك، وانتصروا بما قدرتم من دون الله إن كنتم صادقين في المعارضة. قال القشيري: وكما أن كيد الكافرين يَضْمَحِلُّ في مقابلة معجزات الرسول، فكذلك دعاوى المُلْبِسين تتلاشى عند ظهور أنوار الصديقين. هـ.\nفإن لم تفعلوا ما ذكرنا من المعارضة، ولن تقدروا على ذلك أبداً، فأَذْعنوا، واخْضعوا، واتقوا نار القطيعة والحظوظ، والطمع والهلع، التي مادتها النفوس والفلوس إذ بهما هلك مَن هلك وفاز مَن فاز، أُعدت تلك النار للمنكرين الخصوصية، الجاحدين لوجود التربية النبوية.\nوبَشِّر المصدقين بوجود الخصوصية، المنقادين لأهلها، أن لهم جنات المعارف في الدنيا، وجنات الزخارف في الآخرة، تجري من تحت قلوب أهلها أنوار العلوم والمعارف، فإذا كشف لهم يوم القيامة عن أسرار ذاته، قالوا:\nهذا الذي عرفناه من قبل في دار الدنيا، إذ الوجود واحد والمعرفة متفاوتة، وأتُوا بأرزاق المعارف متشابهة لأن مَنْ عَرَفه في الدنيا عرفه في الآخرة، ومَن أنكره هنا أنكره يوم القيامة، إلا في وقت مخصوص على وجه مخصوص، ولهم في جنات المعارف عرائس المعارف والكشوفات، مطهرات من أدناس الحس وعبث الهوى والشهوات، وهم بعد تمكنهم من شهود الذات، خالدون في عُشّ الحضرة، فيها يسكنون وإليها يأوون.\nوقال القشيري: كما أن أهل الجنة يجدد لهم النعيم في وقت، فالثاني عندهم على ما يظنون كالأول، فإذا ذاقوه وجدوه غير ما تقدم، كذلك أهل الحقائق: أحوالهم في الزيادة أبداً، فإذا رقي أحدهم عن محله، توهم أن الذي سيلقاه في هذا النَّفس مثل ما تقدم، فإذا ذاقه وجده فوق ذلك بأضعاف، كما قال قائلهم:\nمازلت أنزلُ مِنْ وِدادِكَ مَنْزِلاً ... تَتحَيرُ الألبابُ عِندَ نُزُولهِ(1)\nولما ضرب الله الأمثال في القرآن للمنافقين وغيرهم تكلم في ذلك بعض الكفار والملحدين، بينّ الحق تعالى وجه ذلك فقال:","quran_ar":"وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ فِي رَيْبٍ مِمَّا نَزَّلْنا عَلى عَبْدِنا فَأْتُوا بِسُورَةٍ مِنْ مِثْلِهِ وَادْعُوا شُهَداءَكُمْ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (23) فَإِنْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوا وَلَنْ تَفْعَلُوا فَاتَّقُوا النَّارَ الَّتِي وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجارَةُ أُعِدَّتْ لِلْكافِرِينَ (24) وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحاتِ أَنَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهارُ كُلَّما رُزِقُوا مِنْها مِنْ ثَمَرَةٍ رِزْقاً قالُوا هذَا الَّذِي رُزِقْنا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَأُتُوا بِهِ مُتَشابِهاً وَلَهُمْ فِيها أَزْواجٌ مُطَهَّرَةٌ وَهُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (25)","quran_en":"23. If you are in doubt concerning what We have sent down upon Our servant, then bring a sūrah like it, and summon your witnesses apart from God, if you are truthful. 24. But if you do not—and you will never do so—then guard yourselves against the Fire whose fuel is people and stones, prepared for the unbelievers. 25. Give good tidings to those who believe and perform righteous deeds: theirs shall be gardens beneath which rivers flow. Whenever they are provided with fruit from them, they will say, “This is what we were provided with before,” for they shall be given its like. There they shall have purified spouses, and there they shall abide.","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"Conditional doubt and the force of the challenge","html":"<p>Should you ask, “The unbelievers’ doubt concerning the Qurʾān certainly occurred; why, then, is it expressed through <i>in<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إن<\/bdi>), which indicates doubt and uncertainty?”—I say: <i>in<\/i> makes the conditional verb jussive, either in its expressed inflection or in its grammatical position (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">جازمة للفظ الشرط أو محله<\/bdi>), and is assigned to uncertainty about the condition. <i>Idhā<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إذا<\/bdi>), by contrast, does not make the verb jussive in its expressed inflection, but indicates certainty in meaning. Hence the saying:<\/p><blockquote class=\"poetry\">When I doubt with <i>in<\/i>, you find me making jussive;<br>when I am certain with <i>idhā<\/i>, I do not make jussive.<\/blockquote><p>Should you ask, “The unbelievers’ doubt concerning the Qurʾān certainly occurred; why, then, use <i>in<\/i>, which indicates doubt and uncertainty?”—I say: their doubt was misplaced. Had they reflected in the least, it would have disappeared, so clear is the matter and so radiant the proof. Their doubt is therefore treated as though its occurrence were itself doubtful and uncertain.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-29\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B025]<\/a><\/p><p><i>Shuhadāʾ<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الشهداء<\/bdi>) is the plural of <i>shahīd<\/i>, meaning one present, one who bears witness, or a supporter. It is applied to the idols because their worshippers claim that they testify for them. <i>Dūn<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">دون<\/bdi>) originally denotes a place nearer than another thing. It was then borrowed for ranks: “Zayd is below ʿAmr,” that is, in honour. Its use was subsequently extended to any passing from one limit to another or crossing from one affair to another.<\/p><p class=\"translator-note-ref\">[Translator’s print-source notes: <a class=\"noteref\" href=\"#/note/R07-02\">[R07-02]<\/a>]<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"Should you ask, “The unbelievers’ doubt concerning the Qurʾān certainly occurred; why, then, is it expressed through in ( إن ), which indicates doubt and uncertainty?”—I say: in makes the conditional verb jussive, either in its expressed inflection or in its grammatical position ( جازمة للفظ الشرط أو محله ), and is assigned to uncertainty about the condition. Idhā ( إذا ), by contrast, does not make the verb jussive in its expressed inflection, but indicates certainty in meaning. Hence the saying: When I doubt with in , you find me making jussive; when I am certain with idhā , I do not make jussive. Should you ask, “The unbelievers’ doubt concerning the Qurʾān certainly occurred; why, then, use in , which indicates doubt and uncertainty?”—I say: their doubt was misplaced. Had they reflected in the least, it would have disappeared, so clear is the matter and so radiant the proof. Their doubt is therefore treated as though its occurrence were itself doubtful and uncertain. [B025] Shuhadāʾ ( الشهداء ) is the plural of shahīd , meaning one present, one who bears witness, or a supporter. It is applied to the idols because their worshippers claim that they testify for them. Dūn ( دون ) originally denotes a place nearer than another thing. It was then borrowed for ranks: “Zayd is below ʿAmr,” that is, in honour. Its use was subsequently extended to any passing from one limit to another or crossing from one affair to another. [Translator’s print-source notes: [R07-02] ]"},{"type":"exposition","title":"A challenge beyond their power","html":"<p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: if you unbelievers doubt what We have sent down upon Muḥammad—Our servant and Messenger, chosen to receive the mystery of Our revelation—then bring a sūrah of its kind in eloquence and lucid expression, containing sciences, mysteries and disclosures of the unseen such as My Book contains. Summon everyone whose support you can obtain in producing it: the gods that you claim will testify for you on the Day of Resurrection, or the eloquent and accomplished speakers present among you whose assistance you seek apart from God, if you are truthful in claiming that they can benefit you. If you cannot do this—and you never will—then submit and acknowledge the truth. Guard yourselves against the Fire whose fuel is people and stones, meaning sulphur stones: these two are its firewood and fuel. It has been prepared for the unbelievers.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: if you unbelievers doubt what We have sent down upon Muḥammad—Our servant and Messenger, chosen to receive the mystery of Our revelation—then bring a sūrah of its kind in eloquence and lucid expression, containing sciences, mysteries and disclosures of the unseen such as My Book contains. Summon everyone whose support you can obtain in producing it: the gods that you claim will testify for you on the Day of Resurrection, or the eloquent and accomplished speakers present among you whose assistance you seek apart from God, if you are truthful in claiming that they can benefit you. If you cannot do this—and you never will—then submit and acknowledge the truth. Guard yourselves against the Fire whose fuel is people and stones, meaning sulphur stones: these two are its firewood and fuel. It has been prepared for the unbelievers."},{"type":"exposition","title":"The renewed delight of Paradise","html":"<p>Muḥammad—and anyone fit to convey good tidings—give good tidings to those who believe in God and His Messenger and perform the righteous works required of them: theirs are gardens beneath which rivers flow, that is, beneath their palaces. These are rivers of water, honey, milk, and wine delightful to those who drink it. Whenever they are provided with a kind of fruit from them, they say, “This is what we were provided with before,” in the earthly abode. Natural dispositions incline to the familiar: the appearance agrees, while the taste differs. Alternatively, “before” refers to an earlier provision in Paradise. This is explained by the report from the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace: “By Him in whose hand is Muḥammad’s soul, a man in Paradise takes a fruit to eat, and before it has reached his stomach God Most High replaces it with another like it.” Perhaps, then, on seeing it in its former shape, they say this<\/p><p>in astonishment and delight at the immense difference in flavour alongside the close resemblance of appearance. There they have spouses—that is, houris—purified of menstruation and every other defilement, and of blameworthy dispositions and ignoble traits. There they abide for ever, since a delight followed by extinction is embittered for its possessor. As the poet says:<\/p><blockquote class=\"poetry\">There is no good in life while its pleasures are embittered<br>by remembering death and decrepit age.<\/blockquote>","authorial":false,"text":"Muḥammad—and anyone fit to convey good tidings—give good tidings to those who believe in God and His Messenger and perform the righteous works required of them: theirs are gardens beneath which rivers flow, that is, beneath their palaces. These are rivers of water, honey, milk, and wine delightful to those who drink it. Whenever they are provided with a kind of fruit from them, they say, “This is what we were provided with before,” in the earthly abode. Natural dispositions incline to the familiar: the appearance agrees, while the taste differs. Alternatively, “before” refers to an earlier provision in Paradise. This is explained by the report from the Prophet, God bless him and grant him peace: “By Him in whose hand is Muḥammad’s soul, a man in Paradise takes a fruit to eat, and before it has reached his stomach God Most High replaces it with another like it.” Perhaps, then, on seeing it in its former shape, they say this in astonishment and delight at the immense difference in flavour alongside the close resemblance of appearance. There they have spouses—that is, houris—purified of menstruation and every other defilement, and of blameworthy dispositions and ignoble traits. There they abide for ever, since a delight followed by extinction is embittered for its possessor. As the poet says: There is no good in life while its pleasures are embittered by remembering death and decrepit age."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"The challenge addressed to those who deny spiritual election","html":"<p>If you ordinary people doubt the lights with which We have specially favoured Our friend, the forms of knowledge and mysteries We have sent down upon his heart, the splendour and lights manifested upon him, and the righteous and good who have found guidance at his hands, then produce something of this yourselves. Seek all the support you can apart from God, if you are truthful in your opposition. Al-Qushayrī says: “Just as the unbelievers’ plotting dwindles away before the Messenger’s miracles, so the claims of pretenders vanish when the lights of the utterly truthful appear.” End of quotation.<\/p><p>If you do not accomplish the opposition We have mentioned—and you will never be able to do so—then yield and submit. Guard yourselves against the fire of severance, egoic shares, covetousness and anxious grasping, whose substance is souls and money (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">النفوس والفلوس<\/bdi>). Through these two those who perish have perished, and those who triumph have triumphed. That fire is prepared for those who deny special election and reject the existence of Prophetic spiritual formation (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">التربية النبوية<\/bdi>).<\/p><p>Give good tidings to those who affirm the existence of special election and submit to its people: theirs are gardens of gnosis in this world and gardens of adornment in the next. Beneath their inhabitants’ hearts flow the lights of sciences and forms of knowledge. When the mysteries of His Essence are unveiled to them on the Day of Resurrection, they say, “This is what we knew before in the earthly abode,” for existence (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الوجود<\/bdi>) is one, while knowledge of it differs in degree. They are given resembling provisions of gnosis, because one who knew Him here knows Him in the Hereafter; one who denied Him here denies Him on the Day of Resurrection, except at a particular time and in a particular manner.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-30\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B026]<\/a><\/p><p>In the gardens of gnosis they have bridal forms of knowledge and unveiling, purified of the defilements of sense perception and the frivolity of caprice and desires. Once firmly established in witnessing the Essence, they abide in the nest of the Presence: there they dwell, and to it they take refuge.<\/p><p>Al-Qushayrī says: “Just as the people of Paradise receive renewed delight at each moment, imagining the second to be like the first but, on tasting it, finding it unlike what preceded, so the states of the people of realities continually increase. When one rises beyond his station, he imagines that what he will meet in this breath is like what preceded; when he tastes it, he finds it many times greater.” As one of them says:<\/p><blockquote class=\"poetry\">Ever I alight at a dwelling-place of Your love<br>whose approach leaves minds bewildered.<\/blockquote>","authorial":true,"text":"If you ordinary people doubt the lights with which We have specially favoured Our friend, the forms of knowledge and mysteries We have sent down upon his heart, the splendour and lights manifested upon him, and the righteous and good who have found guidance at his hands, then produce something of this yourselves. Seek all the support you can apart from God, if you are truthful in your opposition. Al-Qushayrī says: “Just as the unbelievers’ plotting dwindles away before the Messenger’s miracles, so the claims of pretenders vanish when the lights of the utterly truthful appear.” End of quotation. If you do not accomplish the opposition We have mentioned—and you will never be able to do so—then yield and submit. Guard yourselves against the fire of severance, egoic shares, covetousness and anxious grasping, whose substance is souls and money ( النفوس والفلوس ). Through these two those who perish have perished, and those who triumph have triumphed. That fire is prepared for those who deny special election and reject the existence of Prophetic spiritual formation ( التربية النبوية ). Give good tidings to those who affirm the existence of special election and submit to its people: theirs are gardens of gnosis in this world and gardens of adornment in the next. Beneath their inhabitants’ hearts flow the lights of sciences and forms of knowledge. When the mysteries of His Essence are unveiled to them on the Day of Resurrection, they say, “This is what we knew before in the earthly abode,” for existence ( الوجود ) is one, while knowledge of it differs in degree. They are given resembling provisions of gnosis, because one who knew Him here knows Him in the Hereafter; one who denied Him here denies Him on the Day of Resurrection, except at a particular time and in a particular manner. [B026] In the gardens of gnosis they have bridal forms of knowledge and unveiling, purified of the defilements of sense perception and the frivolity of caprice and desires. Once firmly established in witnessing the Essence, they abide in the nest of the Presence: there they dwell, and to it they take refuge. Al-Qushayrī says: “Just as the people of Paradise receive renewed delight at each moment, imagining the second to be like the first but, on tasting it, finding it unlike what preceded, so the states of the people of realities continually increase. When one rises beyond his station, he imagines that what he will meet in this breath is like what preceded; when he tastes it, he finds it many times greater.” As one of them says: Ever I alight at a dwelling-place of Your love whose approach leaves minds bewildered."},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>When God set forth parables in the Qurʾān concerning the hypocrites and others, some unbelievers and deniers spoke against them. The Real Most High therefore explained their purpose, saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"When God set forth parables in the Qurʾān concerning the hypocrites and others, some unbelievers and deniers spoke against them. The Real Most High therefore explained their purpose, saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[{"id":"C89.1","page":89,"ar":"البيت ذكره البغدادي في تاريخ بغداد ٥/١٣٥ في قصة مع أبي الحسن النوري.","en":"Al-Baghdādī mentions this verse in Tārīkh Baghdād, 5:135, in an account involving Abū al-Ḥasan al-Nūrī.","anchor":"مازلت أنزل من ودادك منزلا تتحير الألباب عند نزوله"}],"english_characters":6591,"arabic_characters":4763},{"id":"q2-26-27","q":"2:26–27","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:26–27 · Parables, the covenant and the disclosure of divine wisdom","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 90–91","cairo":"I:90–91","source_page_first":90,"source_page_last":91,"ar":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَسْتَحْيِي أَنْ يَضْرِبَ مَثَلاً ما بَعُوضَةً فَما فَوْقَها فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا فَيَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فَيَقُولُونَ ماذا أَرادَ اللَّهُ بِهذا مَثَلاً يُضِلُّ بِهِ كَثِيراً وَيَهْدِي بِهِ كَثِيراً وَما يُضِلُّ بِهِ إِلاَّ الْفاسِقِينَ (26) الَّذِينَ يَنْقُضُونَ عَهْدَ اللَّهِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مِيثاقِهِ وَيَقْطَعُونَ ما أَمَرَ اللَّهُ بِهِ أَنْ يُوصَلَ وَيُفْسِدُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ أُولئِكَ هُمُ الْخاسِرُونَ (27)\nقلت: الحياء: خُلُق كريم يمنع صاحبه من ارتكاب ما يعاب به، وفي الحديث: «إنَّ الله حَيِيٌ كَريم» ، و (مثلاً) مفعول، و (ما) نكرة، صفته، و (بعوضة) بدل، والبعوضة: الذباب. وفي الحديث: «لوْ كَانَتِ الدُّنيَا تُسَاوِي عندَ الله جَنَاحَ بعُوضَةٍ مَا سَقَى الكافرَ منها جَرْعَة ماءٍ» ، وقيل: صِغَار البَقِّ، أي: إن الله لا يترك أن يضرب مثلاً- أيّ مثل كان- بعوضة فما فوقها. أو (بعوضة) مفعول أول، و (مثلاً) مفعول ثانٍ، من باب جعل، و (ماذا) إما مبتدأ وخبرِ، على أن (ذا) موصولة، أو مفعولة بأراد على أنها مركبة، و (مثلاً) حال أو تمييز. والفسق: الخروج، يقال:\nفسقت الرطبة إذا خرجت عن قشرها.\nيقول الحق جلّ جلاله: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يترك ترك المستحيي أَنْ يَضْرِبَ مَثَلًا بالخسيس والكبير كالذباب والعنكبوت وغير ذلك. فأما المؤمنون فيتيقَّنُون أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ، وحكمته: إبراز المعاني اللطيفة في قوالب المحسوسات ليسهل الفهم، وأما الكفار فيعترضون ويقولون: مَاذَا أَرادَ اللَّهُ بهذه الأمثال؟ فإن الله منزه عن ضرب الأمثال بهذه الأشياء الخسيسة، قال الله تعالى فِى الرد عليهم: أراد بهذا إضلال قوم بسبب إنكارها، وهداية آخرين بسبب الإيمان بها، وَما يُضِلُّ بذلك المثل إلا الخارجين عن طاعته، الَّذِينَ نقضوا العهد الذي أُخذ عليهم في عالم الذَّرِّ، أو مطلق العهد، وَيَقْطَعُونَ مَا أَمَرَ اللَّهُ بِهِ أَنْ يُوصَلَ من الأنبياء والرسل والأرحام وغيرها، وَيُفْسِدُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ بالمعاصي والتعويق عن الإيمان، أُولئِكَ هُمُ الْخاسِرُونَ الكاملون في الخسران، نعوذ بالله من الخذلان.\nالإشارة: إن الله لا يترك أن يظهر مثلاً من أنوار قدسه بارزاً بقدرته، مرتدياً برداء حكمته، ملتبساً بأسرار ذاته، مَكسُوّاً بأنوار صفاته من الذرة إلى مالا نهاية له، فالمتجلِّي في النملة هو المتجلي في الفيلة، فأما الذين صَدَّقُوا بتجلي الذات في أنوار الصفات، فيقولون: إنه الحق فائضٌ من نور الربوبية، محتجباً برداء الكبرياء وسبحات الألوهية. وأما الجاحدون لظهور نور ذات الربوبية فينكرونه في حال ظهوره، ويقولون: ماذا أراد الله بهذه العوالم الظاهرة؟ فيقول الحق تعالى: أردت ظهور قدرتي وعجائب حكمتي، ليظهر سر ربوبيتي في مظاهر عبوديتي.\nقال الشيخ أبو الحسن رضى الله عنه: «العبودية جوهرة أظهر بها الربوبية» وقيل لأبي الحسن النُّورِي: ما هذه الأماكن والمخلوقات الظاهرة؟ فقال: عز ظاهر وملك قاهر، ومخلوقات ظاهرة به، وصادرة عنه، لا هي متصلة به ولا منفصلة عنه، فرغ من الأشياء ولم تفرغ منه، لأنها تحتاج إليه وهو لا يحتاج إليها. هـ.\nفأراد الله بظهور هذا الكون أن يضل به قوماً فيقفون مع ظاهر غرَّتِه، ويهدي به قوماً فينفذون إلى باطن عبرته. وما يضل به إلا الفاسقين الخارجين عن دائرة الشهود، المنكرين لتجليات الملك المعبود، الذين ينقضون عهد الله، وهو معرفة الروح التي حصلت لها وهي في عالم الذر، ويقطعونَ ما أمر اللهُ به أن يوصل من الشيوخ العارفين، الذين أَهَّلَهُمَ الله للتربية والترقية، وهم لا ينقطعون ما دامت المِلَّةُ المحمدية، ويفسدون في الأرض بالإنكار والتعويق عن طريق الخصوص، بتضييعهم الأصولَ، وهي صحبة العارفين، والتأدب لهم، والتعظيم لحرمتهم. وبالله التوفيق، وهو الهادي إلى سواء الطريق.\nثم عجّب الحقّ تعالى خلقه من خفائه بعد شدة ظهوره، فقال:","quran_ar":"إِنَّ اللَّهَ لا يَسْتَحْيِي أَنْ يَضْرِبَ مَثَلاً ما بَعُوضَةً فَما فَوْقَها فَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا فَيَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّهِمْ وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فَيَقُولُونَ ماذا أَرادَ اللَّهُ بِهذا مَثَلاً يُضِلُّ بِهِ كَثِيراً وَيَهْدِي بِهِ كَثِيراً وَما يُضِلُّ بِهِ إِلاَّ الْفاسِقِينَ (26) الَّذِينَ يَنْقُضُونَ عَهْدَ اللَّهِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مِيثاقِهِ وَيَقْطَعُونَ ما أَمَرَ اللَّهُ بِهِ أَنْ يُوصَلَ وَيُفْسِدُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ أُولئِكَ هُمُ الْخاسِرُونَ (27)","quran_en":"26. God does not refrain through modesty from setting forth a parable of a gnat, or anything beyond it. Those who believe know that it is the truth from their Lord; but those who disbelieve say, “What does God intend by this as a parable?” Through it He leads many astray, and through it He guides many; yet through it He leads none astray except the transgressors: 27. those who break God’s covenant after its binding confirmation, sever what God has commanded to be joined, and cause corruption on earth. They are the losers.","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"Modesty, the parable and transgression","html":"<p>I say: modesty (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الحياء<\/bdi>) is a noble disposition that prevents its possessor from committing something for which he would be reproached. The hadith says, “God is modest and generous.” <i>Mathalan<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مثلاً<\/bdi>) is an object (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مفعول<\/bdi>); <i>mā<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ما<\/bdi>) is an indefinite word qualifying it; and <i>baʿūḍatan<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعوضة<\/bdi>) is an apposition (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بدل<\/bdi>). <i>Baʿūḍa<\/i> is a fly. The hadith says, “Were this world worth the wing of a gnat in God’s sight, He would not give an unbeliever a draught of water from it.” It is also said to mean the smallest biting insects. Thus: God does not refrain from setting forth a parable—whatever sort it may be—of a gnat or anything beyond it.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-31\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B027]<\/a><\/p><p>Alternatively, <i>baʿūḍatan<\/i> is the first object and <i>mathalan<\/i> the second, on the pattern of <i>jaʿala<\/i>, “to make.” <i>Mādhā<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ماذا<\/bdi>) is either a subject and predicate, with <i>dhā<\/i> a relative expression, or the object of “intends,” when the two form a compound interrogative. <i>Mathalan<\/i> is a circumstantial accusative or an accusative of specification (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حال أو تمييز<\/bdi>). Transgression (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفسق<\/bdi>) means going out: one says, “The ripe date <i>fasaqat<\/i>,” when it comes out of its skin.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"I say: modesty ( الحياء ) is a noble disposition that prevents its possessor from committing something for which he would be reproached. The hadith says, “God is modest and generous.” Mathalan ( مثلاً ) is an object ( مفعول ); mā ( ما ) is an indefinite word qualifying it; and baʿūḍatan ( بعوضة ) is an apposition ( بدل ). Baʿūḍa is a fly. The hadith says, “Were this world worth the wing of a gnat in God’s sight, He would not give an unbeliever a draught of water from it.” It is also said to mean the smallest biting insects. Thus: God does not refrain from setting forth a parable—whatever sort it may be—of a gnat or anything beyond it. [B027] Alternatively, baʿūḍatan is the first object and mathalan the second, on the pattern of jaʿala , “to make.” Mādhā ( ماذا ) is either a subject and predicate, with dhā a relative expression, or the object of “intends,” when the two form a compound interrogative. Mathalan is a circumstantial accusative or an accusative of specification ( حال أو تمييز ). Transgression ( الفسق ) means going out: one says, “The ripe date fasaqat ,” when it comes out of its skin."},{"type":"exposition","title":"The purpose of sensible parables","html":"<p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: God does not refrain, as a modest person might, from setting forth a parable through something lowly or something great—a fly, a spider, or anything else. Believers are certain that it is the truth from their Lord. Its wisdom lies in displaying subtle meanings in sensible forms so that understanding becomes easy. Unbelievers, however, object: “What does God intend by these parables? God is too exalted to strike parables through such lowly things.” In answer, God Most High says: He intends thereby to lead one people astray through their rejection, and to guide others through their faith in them. Through such a parable He leads astray only those who depart from obedience to Him: those who break the covenant taken from them in the world of the primordial particles (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">عالم الذر<\/bdi>), or covenant in its unrestricted sense; who sever what God commanded to be joined—prophets, messengers, ties of kinship and other bonds—and corrupt the earth through disobedience and obstructing faith. These are the losers, complete in their loss. We seek refuge in God from abandonment.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: God does not refrain, as a modest person might, from setting forth a parable through something lowly or something great—a fly, a spider, or anything else. Believers are certain that it is the truth from their Lord. Its wisdom lies in displaying subtle meanings in sensible forms so that understanding becomes easy. Unbelievers, however, object: “What does God intend by these parables? God is too exalted to strike parables through such lowly things.” In answer, God Most High says: He intends thereby to lead one people astray through their rejection, and to guide others through their faith in them. Through such a parable He leads astray only those who depart from obedience to Him: those who break the covenant taken from them in the world of the primordial particles ( عالم الذر ), or covenant in its unrestricted sense; who sever what God commanded to be joined—prophets, messengers, ties of kinship and other bonds—and corrupt the earth through disobedience and obstructing faith. These are the losers, complete in their loss. We seek refuge in God from abandonment."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"Self-disclosure in the smallest and greatest things","html":"<p>God does not refrain from manifesting a similitude of the lights of His holiness, brought forth by His power, clad in the robe of His wisdom, invested with the mysteries of His Essence and clothed in the lights of His attributes—from the smallest particle to that which has no limit. He who discloses Himself in the ant is He who discloses Himself in the elephant. Those who affirm the Essence’s self-disclosure in the lights of the attributes say: it is the Real, flowing forth from the light of lordship, veiled in the robe of majesty and the splendours of divinity. Those who deny the manifestation of the light of the Essence of lordship reject it in its manifestation and say, “What did God intend by these manifest worlds?” The Real Most High replies: “I intended the manifestation of My power and the wonders of My wisdom, so that the mystery of My lordship might appear in the loci of My servanthood.”<\/p><p>Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan, God be pleased with him, said: “Servanthood is a jewel through which He manifested lordship.” Abū al-Ḥasan al-Nūrī was asked, “What are these places and manifest creatures?” He replied: “Manifest might, overpowering dominion, and creatures made manifest through Him and issuing from Him: neither connected to Him nor separated from Him. He has finished with things, but they have not finished with Him, for they need Him while He does not need them.” End of quotation.<\/p><p>By manifesting this cosmos, God intends that one people be led astray through it, stopping at its outward allure, and another be guided through it, penetrating to the inward lesson it offers. None is led astray through it except those who transgress beyond the circle of witnessing and deny the self-disclosures of the worshipped King; those who break God’s covenant, namely the spirit’s knowledge acquired while it was in the world of the primordial particles; and those who sever the bond God commanded to be maintained with the knowing shaykhs whom He qualified for spiritual formation and elevation. Such shaykhs will not cease to exist as long as the Muḥammadan religion remains. These people corrupt the earth through denial and obstruction of the path of the elect, neglecting its foundations: companionship with the gnostics, observing proper courtesy towards them, and honouring their sanctity. Through God is success, and He guides to the even way.<\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"God does not refrain from manifesting a similitude of the lights of His holiness, brought forth by His power, clad in the robe of His wisdom, invested with the mysteries of His Essence and clothed in the lights of His attributes—from the smallest particle to that which has no limit. He who discloses Himself in the ant is He who discloses Himself in the elephant. Those who affirm the Essence’s self-disclosure in the lights of the attributes say: it is the Real, flowing forth from the light of lordship, veiled in the robe of majesty and the splendours of divinity. Those who deny the manifestation of the light of the Essence of lordship reject it in its manifestation and say, “What did God intend by these manifest worlds?” The Real Most High replies: “I intended the manifestation of My power and the wonders of My wisdom, so that the mystery of My lordship might appear in the loci of My servanthood.” Shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan, God be pleased with him, said: “Servanthood is a jewel through which He manifested lordship.” Abū al-Ḥasan al-Nūrī was asked, “What are these places and manifest creatures?” He replied: “Manifest might, overpowering dominion, and creatures made manifest through Him and issuing from Him: neither connected to Him nor separated from Him. He has finished with things, but they have not finished with Him, for they need Him while He does not need them.” End of quotation. By manifesting this cosmos, God intends that one people be led astray through it, stopping at its outward allure, and another be guided through it, penetrating to the inward lesson it offers. None is led astray through it except those who transgress beyond the circle of witnessing and deny the self-disclosures of the worshipped King; those who break God’s covenant, namely the spirit’s knowledge acquired while it was in the world of the primordial particles; and those who sever the bond God commanded to be maintained with the knowing shaykhs whom He qualified for spiritual formation and elevation. Such shaykhs will not cease to exist as long as the Muḥammadan religion remains. These people corrupt the earth through denial and obstruction of the path of the elect, neglecting its foundations: companionship with the gnostics, observing proper courtesy towards them, and honouring their sanctity. Through God is success, and He guides to the even way."},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>The Real Most High then calls His creatures to wonder at His hiddenness despite His overwhelming manifestation, saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real Most High then calls His creatures to wonder at His hiddenness despite His overwhelming manifestation, saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[],"english_characters":4702,"arabic_characters":3272},{"id":"q2-28","q":"2:28","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:28 · Life, death and return","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 91–92","cairo":"I:91–92","source_page_first":91,"source_page_last":92,"ar":"كَيْفَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَكُنْتُمْ أَمْواتاً فَأَحْياكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيكُمْ ثُمَّ إِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ (28)\nقلت: (كيف) حال لأنها وقعت قبل كلام تام.\nيقول الحق جلّ جلاله: كَيْفَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِاللَّهِ وتجحدون نعمه المتوالية، وَالحالة أنكم كُنْتُمْ أَمْواتاً نطفاً في الأرحام، فَأَحْياكُمْ بنفخ الروح في أجسادكم، ثُمَّ يُمِيتُكُمْ عند انقضاء آجالكم، ثُمَّ يُحْيِيكُمْ عند البعث لحسابكم، ثم يسكنكم دار القرار، إمّا إلى الجنة وإمّا إلى النار. فهذه الآثار دالّة على باهر قدرته وتمام حكمته، فقد وضح الحق وظهر، فَمَنْ شاءَ فَلْيُؤْمِنْ وَمَنْ شاءَ فَلْيَكْفُرْ.\nالإشارة: كيف تنكرون ظهور نور الحق في الأكوان، وتبعدون عن حضرة الشهود والعيان، وقد كنتم أمواتاً بالغفلة وغم الحجاب، فأحياكم باليقظة والإياب، ثم يميتكم بالفناء عن شهود ما سواه، ثم يحييكم بالرجوع إلى شهود أثره بالله، ثم إليه ترجعون في كل شيء لشهود نوره في كل شيء، وقبل كل شيء، وبعد كل شيء، وعند كل شيء «كان الله ولا شيء معه، وهو الآن على ما عليه كان» .\nولمَّا ذكر نعمة الإيجاد أتبعها بنعمة الإمداد، فقال:","quran_ar":"كَيْفَ تَكْفُرُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَكُنْتُمْ أَمْواتاً فَأَحْياكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيكُمْ ثُمَّ إِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ (28)","quran_en":"28. How can you disbelieve in God, when you were lifeless and He gave you life? Then He will cause you to die, then give you life again; then to Him you shall be returned.","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"The circumstantial force of “how”","html":"<p>I say: “How” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">كيف<\/bdi>) has the force of a circumstantial expression (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حال<\/bdi>), because it precedes a complete statement.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"I say: “How” ( كيف ) has the force of a circumstantial expression ( حال ), because it precedes a complete statement."},{"type":"exposition","title":"The successive gifts of life","html":"<p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: how can you disbelieve in God and deny His successive blessings, when you were lifeless—drops in the wombs—and He gave you life by breathing the spirit into your bodies? Then He causes you to die when your appointed terms expire; then He gives you life at the resurrection for your reckoning. Thereafter He settles you in the enduring abode, either Paradise or the Fire. These effects indicate His dazzling power and perfect wisdom. The truth has become clear and manifest: “Whoever wills, let him believe; and whoever wills, let him disbelieve” [18:29].<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: how can you disbelieve in God and deny His successive blessings, when you were lifeless—drops in the wombs—and He gave you life by breathing the spirit into your bodies? Then He causes you to die when your appointed terms expire; then He gives you life at the resurrection for your reckoning. Thereafter He settles you in the enduring abode, either Paradise or the Fire. These effects indicate His dazzling power and perfect wisdom. The truth has become clear and manifest: “Whoever wills, let him believe; and whoever wills, let him disbelieve” [18:29]."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"Awakening, effacement and renewed witnessing","html":"<p>How can you deny the manifestation of the Real’s light in created things and remain distant from the presence of witnessing and direct vision, when you were dead through heedlessness and the gloom of the veil, and He gave you life through awakening and return? Then He causes you to die through effacement from witnessing anything other than Him; then He gives you life through returning, by God, to witness His effect. Then to Him you return in everything, witnessing His light in everything, before everything, after everything and with everything: “God was, and nothing was with Him; and He is now as He was.”<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-32\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B028]<\/a><\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"How can you deny the manifestation of the Real’s light in created things and remain distant from the presence of witnessing and direct vision, when you were dead through heedlessness and the gloom of the veil, and He gave you life through awakening and return? Then He causes you to die through effacement from witnessing anything other than Him; then He gives you life through returning, by God, to witness His effect. Then to Him you return in everything, witnessing His light in everything, before everything, after everything and with everything: “God was, and nothing was with Him; and He is now as He was.” [B028]"},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>After mentioning the blessing of bringing into existence (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الإيجاد<\/bdi>), He follows it with the blessing of sustaining provision (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الإمداد<\/bdi>), saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"After mentioning the blessing of bringing into existence ( الإيجاد ), He follows it with the blessing of sustaining provision ( الإمداد ), saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[],"english_characters":1476,"arabic_characters":977},{"id":"q2-29","q":"2:29","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:29 · Creation for the human being and the seven spiritual stations","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 92–93","cairo":"I:92–93","source_page_first":92,"source_page_last":93,"ar":"هُوَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ لَكُمْ ما فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعاً ثُمَّ اسْتَوى إِلَى السَّماءِ فَسَوَّاهُنَّ سَبْعَ سَماواتٍ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ (29)\nقلت: جَمِيعاً حال مؤكدة من ما، وثُمَّ للترتيب الذكري لا الخارجي(1) لأن دحو الأرض مؤخر عن خلق السماء، إلا أن يكون العطف على معنى الجملة، والتقدير: هُوَ الذى خَلَقَ لَكُمْ الأرض مشتملة على جميع منافعكم، ثم استوى إلى السماء فخلقهن سبعاً، ثم دحا الأرض وبسطها.\nوالتسوية: خلق الأشياء سالمة من العوج والخلل، و (سبع) : بدل من الضمير، أو بيان له، وجملة وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ تعليل لِما قبله. أي: ولكونه عالماً بكنه الأشياء كلها خلق ما خلق على هذا النمط الأكمل والوجه الأنفع.\nيقول الحق جلّ جلاله على لسان الواسطة: هُوَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ لأجلكم ما استقر فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعاً تنتفعون به في الظاهر قوتاً لأشباحكم، ودواء لأبدانكم، ومتعة لنفوسكم، وتنتفعون به في الباطن بالتفكر والاعتبار، وزيادة في إيمانكم وقوة لإيقانكم، ثم قصد إِلَى السَّماءِ قصد إرادة، فخلقهن سَبْعَ سَماواتٍ مستوية تامة، ليس فيها تفاوت ولا خلل، تظلكم بجرمها، وتضيء عليكم بشمسها وقمرها وكواكبها، وقد أحاط علمه بالأشياء كلها، فلذلك خلقها على هذا النمط الغريب والإتقان العجيب.\nالإشارة: يا عبادي خلقتُ الأشياء كُلَّها من أجلكم، الأرض تُقلكم، والسماء تُظلكم، والجهات تَكْتَنِفُكُمْ والحيوانات تخدُمكم، والنباتات تنفعكم، وخلقتكم من أجلي، فكيف تميلون إلى غيري، وتنسَوْن إحساني وبرِّي؟!! الأشياء كلها عبيدكم وأنتم عبيد الحضرة، «أنت مع الأكوان ما لم تشهد المكون، فإذا شهدت المكون كانت الأكوان معك» .\nوفي بعض الكتب المنزلة يقول الله تعالى: (يا عبدي إنما منحتك صفاتي لتعرفني بها، فإن ادعيتها لنفسك سلبتُك الولاية، ولم أسلبك صفاتي، يا عبدي: أنت صفتي وأنا صفتك، فارجع إليَّ أرجع إليك، يا عبدي: فيك للعلوم باب مفتاحه أنا، وفيك للجهل باب مفتاحه أنت، فاقصد أيّ البابين شئت، يا عبدي: قربي منك بقدر بعدك عن نفسك وبعدي عنك بقدر قربك من نفسك، فقد عرفتك الطريق، فاترك نفسك تصل إليَّ في خطرة واحدة، يا عبدي: كل ما جمعك علي فهو مني، وكل ما فرقك عني فهو منك، فجاهد نفسك تصل إليّ، وإني لغني عن العالمين، يا عبدي: إن منحتني نفسك رددتها إليك راضية مرضية، وإن تركتها عندك فهي أعظم بلية، فهي أعدى الأعادي إليك فجاهدها تَعُدْ بالفوائد إليك) .\nوفي بعض الآثار المروية عن الله تعالى: «يا عبدي: أنا بُدُّك اللازم فالزم بُدَّك»(1). ويمكن أن يشار بالأرض إلى أرض العبودية، وبالسماء إلى سماء الحقيقة، وبالسبع سموات إلى سبع مقامات وهي الصبر والشكر والتوكل والرضى والتسليم والمحبة والمعرفة. والله تعالى أعلم.\nولما ذكر خلق العالم العلوي والسفلي، ذكر كيفية ابتداء من عمَّر العالم السفليَّ من جنس الآدمي، فقال:","quran_ar":"هُوَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ لَكُمْ ما فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعاً ثُمَّ اسْتَوى إِلَى السَّماءِ فَسَوَّاهُنَّ سَبْعَ سَماواتٍ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ (29)","quran_en":"29. He it is who created for you all that is on earth; then He turned to the heaven and fashioned them as seven heavens. He knows all things.","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"The order of mention and the order of creation","html":"<p>I say: “all” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">جميعاً<\/bdi>) is an emphatic circumstantial expression (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حال مؤكدة<\/bdi>) referring to “what.” “Then” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ثم<\/bdi>) indicates order in the account, not necessarily order in external occurrence (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الترتيب الذكري لا الخارجي<\/bdi>), because the spreading of the earth came after the creation of heaven. An alternative is that the coordination refers to the sentence’s sense, giving the reconstruction: He it is who created the earth for you, containing all your benefits; then He turned to heaven and created the seven; then He spread and extended the earth.<\/p><p>Fashioning or setting in order (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">التسوية<\/bdi>) means creating things free from crookedness and defect. “Seven” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">سبع<\/bdi>) is an apposition to the pronoun or an explanatory specification of it (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بدل أو بيان<\/bdi>). “He knows all things” explains what precedes: because He knows the inmost reality of all things, He created what He created according to this most perfect pattern and most beneficial manner.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"I say: “all” ( جميعاً ) is an emphatic circumstantial expression ( حال مؤكدة ) referring to “what.” “Then” ( ثم ) indicates order in the account, not necessarily order in external occurrence ( الترتيب الذكري لا الخارجي ), because the spreading of the earth came after the creation of heaven. An alternative is that the coordination refers to the sentence’s sense, giving the reconstruction: He it is who created the earth for you, containing all your benefits; then He turned to heaven and created the seven; then He spread and extended the earth. Fashioning or setting in order ( التسوية ) means creating things free from crookedness and defect. “Seven” ( سبع ) is an apposition to the pronoun or an explanatory specification of it ( بدل أو بيان ). “He knows all things” explains what precedes: because He knows the inmost reality of all things, He created what He created according to this most perfect pattern and most beneficial manner."},{"type":"exposition","title":"Outward benefit and inward reflection","html":"<p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, says through the tongue of the intermediary: He created for your sake everything established on earth. Outwardly you benefit from it as sustenance for your bodies, medicine for your physical frames and enjoyment for your souls; inwardly you benefit through reflection and taking heed, an increase of faith and strengthening of certainty. He then directed Himself towards the heaven with the intention of His will and created them as seven heavens, well-formed and complete, without disparity or defect. Their mass overshadows you, and their sun, moon and stars give you light. His knowledge encompasses all things; hence He created them according to this wondrous pattern and marvellous perfection.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says through the tongue of the intermediary: He created for your sake everything established on earth. Outwardly you benefit from it as sustenance for your bodies, medicine for your physical frames and enjoyment for your souls; inwardly you benefit through reflection and taking heed, an increase of faith and strengthening of certainty. He then directed Himself towards the heaven with the intention of His will and created them as seven heavens, well-formed and complete, without disparity or defect. Their mass overshadows you, and their sun, moon and stars give you light. His knowledge encompasses all things; hence He created them according to this wondrous pattern and marvellous perfection."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"Created things serve you; you belong to the Presence","html":"<p>My servants, I created all things for your sake. The earth bears you, heaven overshadows you, the directions encompass you, animals serve you and plants benefit you. I created you for My sake: how, then, can you incline to another and forget My kindness and beneficence? All things are your servants, while you are servants of the Presence. “You are with created things so long as you do not witness their Creator; when you witness the Creator, created things are with you.”<\/p><p>In one of the revealed books, God Most High says: “My servant, I only bestowed My attributes upon you so that you might know Me through them. If you claim them for yourself, I deprive you of friendship with Me, though I do not deprive you of My attributes. My servant, you are My attribute, and I am your attribute: return to Me and I return to you. My servant, within you is a gate to the sciences whose key is I; and within you is a gate to ignorance whose key is you. Seek whichever gate you wish. My servant, My nearness to you is in proportion to your distance from yourself, and My distance from you is in proportion to your nearness to yourself. I have shown you the way: leave yourself and reach Me in a single movement of thought. My servant, whatever gathers you unto Me comes from Me; whatever scatters you away from Me comes from you. Strive against yourself and reach Me: I have no need of the worlds. My servant, if you grant Me your soul, I return it to you content and well-pleasing; if you keep it with yourself, it is your greatest affliction and your most hostile enemy. Strive against it, and it returns to you bringing benefits.”<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-33\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B029]<\/a><\/p><p>Among the reports transmitted from God Most High is: “My servant, I am your indispensable need: cleave, then, to that without which you cannot be.” The earth may also allude to the earth of servanthood, heaven to the heaven of reality, and the seven heavens to seven stations: patience, thankfulness, reliance, contentment, surrender, love and gnosis (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الصبر والشكر والتوكل والرضى والتسليم والمحبة والمعرفة<\/bdi>). And God Most High knows best.<\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"My servants, I created all things for your sake. The earth bears you, heaven overshadows you, the directions encompass you, animals serve you and plants benefit you. I created you for My sake: how, then, can you incline to another and forget My kindness and beneficence? All things are your servants, while you are servants of the Presence. “You are with created things so long as you do not witness their Creator; when you witness the Creator, created things are with you.” In one of the revealed books, God Most High says: “My servant, I only bestowed My attributes upon you so that you might know Me through them. If you claim them for yourself, I deprive you of friendship with Me, though I do not deprive you of My attributes. My servant, you are My attribute, and I am your attribute: return to Me and I return to you. My servant, within you is a gate to the sciences whose key is I; and within you is a gate to ignorance whose key is you. Seek whichever gate you wish. My servant, My nearness to you is in proportion to your distance from yourself, and My distance from you is in proportion to your nearness to yourself. I have shown you the way: leave yourself and reach Me in a single movement of thought. My servant, whatever gathers you unto Me comes from Me; whatever scatters you away from Me comes from you. Strive against yourself and reach Me: I have no need of the worlds. My servant, if you grant Me your soul, I return it to you content and well-pleasing; if you keep it with yourself, it is your greatest affliction and your most hostile enemy. Strive against it, and it returns to you bringing benefits.” [B029] Among the reports transmitted from God Most High is: “My servant, I am your indispensable need: cleave, then, to that without which you cannot be.” The earth may also allude to the earth of servanthood, heaven to the heaven of reality, and the seven heavens to seven stations: patience, thankfulness, reliance, contentment, surrender, love and gnosis ( الصبر والشكر والتوكل والرضى والتسليم والمحبة والمعرفة ). And God Most High knows best."},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>Having mentioned the creation of the upper and lower worlds, He recounts how the human kind that populated the lower world first began, saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"Having mentioned the creation of the upper and lower worlds, He recounts how the human kind that populated the lower world first began, saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[{"id":"C92.1","page":92,"ar":"أي: ترتيب الإخبار لا ترتيب الأمر في نفسه.","en":"That is, the order in which the account is told, rather than the order of the matter itself.","anchor":"وثم للترتيب الذكري لا الخارجي"},{"id":"C93.1","page":93,"ar":"أخرجه الديلمي في الفردوس (٥/٢٣٠ ح ٨٠٤٠) عن أنس مرفوعا. ورواه الخطيب في تاريخ بغداد ٢/٢٤٢ وقال: هذا الحديث موضوع المتن.","en":"Al-Daylamī records it in al-Firdaws (5:230, report 8040), from Anas, as a report attributed to the Prophet. Al-Khaṭīb also relates it in Tārīkh Baghdād, 2:242, and says: “The text of this hadith is fabricated.”","anchor":"يا عبدي أنا بدك اللازم فالزم بدك"}],"english_characters":3888,"arabic_characters":2377},{"id":"q2-30-33","q":"2:30–33","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:30–33 · Adam, the names and the dignity of knowledge","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 93–95","cairo":"I:93–95","source_page_first":93,"source_page_last":95,"ar":"وَإِذْ قالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلائِكَةِ إِنِّي جاعِلٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً قالُوا أَتَجْعَلُ فِيها مَنْ يُفْسِدُ فِيها وَيَسْفِكُ الدِّماءَ وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ قالَ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ ما لا تَعْلَمُونَ (30) وَعَلَّمَ آدَمَ الْأَسْماءَ كُلَّها ثُمَّ عَرَضَهُمْ عَلَى الْمَلائِكَةِ فَقالَ أَنْبِئُونِي بِأَسْماءِ هؤُلاءِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (31) قالُوا سُبْحانَكَ لا عِلْمَ لَنا إِلاَّ مَا عَلَّمْتَنا إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَلِيمُ الْحَكِيمُ (32) قالَ يَا آدَمُ أَنْبِئْهُمْ بِأَسْمائِهِمْ فَلَمَّا أَنْبَأَهُمْ بِأَسْمائِهِمْ قالَ أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَأَعْلَمُ ما تُبْدُونَ وَما كُنْتُمْ تَكْتُمُونَ (33)\nلمّا أراد الله تعالى عمارة الأرض، بعد أن عمر السموات بالملائكة، أخبر الملائكة بما هو صانع من ذلك تنويهاً بآدم وتشريفاً لذريته، وتعليما لعباده أمر المشاورة، فقال لهم: إِنِّي جاعِلٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً يخلفني في أرضي وتنفيذ أحكامي، قالُوا على وجه الاستفهام، أو من الإدلال، إِن كَانَ مِنَ المقربين، بعد أن رأوا الجن قد أفسدوا وسفكوا الدماء: أَتَجْعَلُ فِيها مَنْ يُفْسِدُ فِيها، وشأن الخليفة الإصلاح، وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ، أي: نسبح ملتبسين بحمدك، وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ، أي: نطهر أنفسنا لأجلك، أو ننزهك عما لا يليق بجلال قدسك، فنحن أحق بالخلافة منهم.\nقال الحقّ جلّ وعلا: إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ..... ما لا تَعْلَمُونَ فإني أعلم أنه يكون منهم رسل وأنبياء وأولياء، ومن يكون مثلكم أو أعظم منكم، ولما ألقى الخليل في النار ضجت الملائكة وقالت: «يا رب هذا خليلك يحرق بالنار» .\nفقال لهم: «إن استغاث بكم فأغيثوه» . فلما رفع همَّتَه عنهم قال الحق تعالى: أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ ما لا تعلمون.\nثم وَجَّهَ الحق تعالى استحقاقه للخلافة وهو تشريفه بالعلم، فقال: وَعَلَّمَ آدَمَ الْأَسْماءَ كُلَّها، أي: مسميات الأسماء بأن ألقى في رُوعه ما تحتاج إليه ذريته من اللغات والحروف، وخواص الأشياء ومنافعها، ثم عرض تلك المسميات على الملائكة، إظهاراً لعجزهم، وتشريفاً لآدم بالعلم، فَقالَ: أخبروني بِأَسْماءِ هؤُلاءِ المسميات إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ في ادعائكم استحقاق الخلافة، فلما عجزوا عن معرفة تلك الأسماء قالُوا سُبْحانَكَ أي: تنزيهاً لك عن العبث، لا عِلْمَ لَنا إِلَّا مَا عَلَّمْتَنا إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَلِيمُ بكل شيء، الْحَكِيمُ لإتقانك كل شيء، وهذا اعتراف منهم بالقصور والعجز، وإشعار بأن سؤالهم كان استفهاماً وطلباً لتفسير ما أشكل عليهم، ولم يكن اعتراضاً.\nقال الحق جلّ جلاله: يَا آدَمُ أَنْبِئْهُمْ بِأَسْمائِهِمْ، وعيِّن لهم اسم كل مسمى، فلما أخبرهم بذلك بحيث قال مثلاً: هذا فرس وهذا جمل، وعين ذلك لهم، وظهرت ميزته عليهم بالعلم حتى استحق الخلافة، قال الحقّ تعالى: أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ أي: ما غاب، وأعلم ما تظهرونه من قولكم:\nأَتَجْعَلُ فِيها.. الخ، وما تكتمونه من استحقاقكم الخلافة، وقولكم: لن يخلق الله تعالى أحداً أعلم منا لتقدمنا، والفضل لمن صدق لا لمن سبق.\nقال البيضاوي: اعلم أن هذه الآيات تدل على شرف الإنسان، ومزية العلم وفضله على العبادة، وأنه شرط في الخلافة، بل العمدة فيها، وأن التعليم يصح إطلاقه عليه تعالى، وإن لم يصح إطلاق المعلم عليه لاختصاصه بمن يحترف به، وأن اللغات توقيفية- علمها الله بالوحي-، وأن آدم عليه السلام أفضل من هؤلاء الملائكة لأنه أعلم منهم، والأعلم أفضل لقوله تعالى: هَلْ يَسْتَوِي الَّذِينَ يَعْلَمُونَ وَالَّذِينَ لاَ يَعْلَمُونَ، وأن الله يعلم الأشياء قبل حدوثها. هـ. باختصار.\nوقال في تفسير الملائكة: إنهم أجسام لطيفة قادرة على التشكل، وهي منقسمة على قسمين: قسم شأنهم الاستغراق في معرفة الحق والتنزه عن الاشتغال بغيره، - وهم العليِّون، والملائكة المقربون- وقسم يدبرون الأمر مِنَ\nالسماء إلى الأرض على ما ثبت به القضاء وجرى به القلم الإلهي، وهم المدبرات أمراً، فمنهم سماوية، ومنهم أرضية. هـ. مختصراً.\nالإشارة: اعلم أن الروح القائمة بهذا الآدمي هي قطعة من الروح الأعظم التي هي المعاني القائمة بالأواني، وهي آدم الأكبر والأب الأقدم، وفي ذلك يقول ابن الفارض:\nوإنِّي وإنْ كنتُ ابن آدمَ صُورةً ... فلِي فِيه مَعْنىً شاهدٌ بأُبوَّتِي\nفلما أراد الحق تعالى أن يستخلف هذا الروح في هذه البشرية لتدبرها وتصرفها فيما أريد منها، قالت الملائكة بلسان حالها: كيف تجعل فيها من يفسد فيها بالميل إلى الحظوظ والشهوات، ويسفك الدماء بالغضب والحميات، ونحن نسبحك وننزهك عما لا يليق بك؟ رأت الملائكة ما يصدر من بعض الأرواح من الميل إلى الحضيض الأسفل، ولم تر ما يصدر من بعضها من التصفية والترقية، فقال لهم الحق تعالى: إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ ما لا تَعْلَمُونَ فإن منها من تعرج إلى عرش الحضرة، وتعبدني بالفكرة والنظرة، وتستولي على الوجود بأسره، وتنكشف لها عند ذلك أسرار الذات وأنوار الصفات وأسماء المسميات.\nفيقول الحق تعالى للملائكة: هل فيكم من كشف له عن هذا السر المكنون، والاسم المصون، فقالوا: سُبْحانَكَ لا عِلْمَ لَنا إِلَّا ما عَلَّمْتَنا من علم الصفات دون أسرار الذات إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَلِيمُ الْحَكِيمُ يقول الحق تعالى لروح العارف التي نفذت إلى بحر وحدة الذات وتيار الصفات: أنبئهم بما غاب عنهم من أسرار الجبروت، وأسماء الملكوت، فلما أعلمهم بما كوشف له من الأسرار، وانفلق له من الأنوار، أقروا بشرف الآدمي، وسجدوا لطلعة آدم عليه السلام فقال الحق لهم: أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ؟ أي: ما غاب في سماء الأرواح من الأسرار وفي أرض النفوس من الأنوار، وأعلم ما تظهرونه من الانقياد، وما تكتمونه من الاعتقاد، والله تعالى أعلم.\nولما تبينّ شرف آدم عليه السلام وبان فضله أمرهم بالسجود له، فقال:","quran_ar":"وَإِذْ قالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلائِكَةِ إِنِّي جاعِلٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً قالُوا أَتَجْعَلُ فِيها مَنْ يُفْسِدُ فِيها وَيَسْفِكُ الدِّماءَ وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ قالَ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ ما لا تَعْلَمُونَ (30) وَعَلَّمَ آدَمَ الْأَسْماءَ كُلَّها ثُمَّ عَرَضَهُمْ عَلَى الْمَلائِكَةِ فَقالَ أَنْبِئُونِي بِأَسْماءِ هؤُلاءِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صادِقِينَ (31) قالُوا سُبْحانَكَ لا عِلْمَ لَنا إِلاَّ مَا عَلَّمْتَنا إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَلِيمُ الْحَكِيمُ (32) قالَ يَا آدَمُ أَنْبِئْهُمْ بِأَسْمائِهِمْ فَلَمَّا أَنْبَأَهُمْ بِأَسْمائِهِمْ قالَ أَلَمْ أَقُلْ لَكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّماواتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَأَعْلَمُ ما تُبْدُونَ وَما كُنْتُمْ تَكْتُمُونَ (33)","quran_en":"30. When your Lord said to the angels, “I am placing a vicegerent on earth,” they said, “Will You place there one who causes corruption and sheds blood, while we glorify You with praise and proclaim Your holiness?” He said, “I know what you do not know.” 31. He taught Adam all the names; then He presented them to the angels and said, “Tell Me the names of these, if you are truthful.” 32. They said, “Glory be to You! We have no knowledge except what You have taught us. You are indeed the Knowing, the Wise.” 33. He said, “Adam, tell them their names.” When he had told them their names, He said, “Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and earth, and know what you disclose and what you used to conceal?”","segments":[{"type":"exposition","title":"The angels’ question and the purpose of vicegerency","html":"<p>When God Most High willed to populate the earth, having populated the heavens with angels, He informed the angels of what He would do, to extol Adam, honour his offspring, and teach His servants the practice of consultation. He told them: “I am placing on earth a vicegerent (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">خليفة<\/bdi>) who represents Me there and executes My judgements.” They replied by way of inquiry—or with the intimacy of confidence, if the speaker was among those brought near—after seeing the jinn corrupt and shed blood: “Will You place there one who causes corruption,” when a vicegerent’s task is to put things right, “while we glorify You with praise,” that is, glorify You accompanied by praising You, “and sanctify ourselves for You,” purifying ourselves for Your sake or declaring You free of whatever does not befit Your holy majesty? Thus: we are more entitled to vicegerency than they are.<\/p><p>The Real, exalted and sublime, replied: “I know what you do not know.” I know that among them will be messengers, prophets and friends of God, and those who are your equals or greater than you. When the Friend, Abraham, was cast into the fire, the angels cried out, “Lord, this is Your friend being burned!” He told them, “If he seeks your help, help him.” When Abraham raised his aspiration beyond them, the Real Most High said, “Did I not tell you that I know what you do not know?”<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"When God Most High willed to populate the earth, having populated the heavens with angels, He informed the angels of what He would do, to extol Adam, honour his offspring, and teach His servants the practice of consultation. He told them: “I am placing on earth a vicegerent ( خليفة ) who represents Me there and executes My judgements.” They replied by way of inquiry—or with the intimacy of confidence, if the speaker was among those brought near—after seeing the jinn corrupt and shed blood: “Will You place there one who causes corruption,” when a vicegerent’s task is to put things right, “while we glorify You with praise,” that is, glorify You accompanied by praising You, “and sanctify ourselves for You,” purifying ourselves for Your sake or declaring You free of whatever does not befit Your holy majesty? Thus: we are more entitled to vicegerency than they are. The Real, exalted and sublime, replied: “I know what you do not know.” I know that among them will be messengers, prophets and friends of God, and those who are your equals or greater than you. When the Friend, Abraham, was cast into the fire, the angels cried out, “Lord, this is Your friend being burned!” He told them, “If he seeks your help, help him.” When Abraham raised his aspiration beyond them, the Real Most High said, “Did I not tell you that I know what you do not know?”"},{"type":"theology","title":"The names, humility and the priority of knowledge","html":"<p>The Real Most High then disclosed the ground of Adam’s entitlement to vicegerency: his ennoblement through knowledge. “He taught Adam all the names,” that is, the things named. He cast into Adam’s heart the languages and letters, and the properties and benefits of things, that his descendants would require. He then displayed these named things to the angels, revealing their inability and honouring Adam through knowledge. He said: tell Me the names of these things, if you are truthful in your claim to deserve vicegerency.<\/p><p>When they could not recognize those names, they replied, “Glory be to You”—we declare You free from purposeless action—“we have no knowledge except what You taught us. You are the Knowing,” of everything, “the Wise,” in Your perfect ordering of everything. This acknowledges their limitation and inability and indicates that their question was an inquiry seeking explanation of what they found difficult, not an objection.<\/p><p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, said: “Adam, tell them their names,” specifying for them the name of each named thing. When he told them—for example, “This is a horse, and this a camel”—and distinguished these things for them, his excellence over them in knowledge became evident, establishing his entitlement to vicegerency. The Real Most High said: “Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and earth”—what is hidden—and know what you reveal in saying, “Will You place there…?” and what you conceal concerning your own entitlement to vicegerency, and your saying, “God will not create anyone more knowledgeable than us, since we came before”? Excellence belongs to the one who is true, not simply to the one who came first.<\/p><p>Al-Bayḍāwī says: “Know that these verses indicate the dignity of the human being, the distinction of knowledge and its superiority to worship, and that knowledge is a condition of vicegerency—indeed, its principal foundation. They indicate that ‘teaching’ may be predicated of God, although He may not be called ‘a teacher’ (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المعلّم<\/bdi>), since that designation belongs particularly to someone who practises it as a profession; that languages are divinely instituted (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">توقيفية<\/bdi>), taught by God through revelation; and that Adam, peace be upon him, is superior to these angels because he knows more than they do. The more knowledgeable is superior, according to His words, ‘Are those who know equal to those who do not know?’ [39:9]. They also indicate that God knows things before they occur.” End of the abridged quotation.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-34\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B030]<\/a><\/p><p>In explaining the angels, he says: “They are subtle bodies (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أجسام لطيفة<\/bdi>) capable of assuming forms and are divided into two classes. One is wholly absorbed in knowing the Real and free from occupying itself with anything else: these are the exalted ones and the angels brought near. The other administers affairs from<\/p><p>heaven to earth according to the established decree and the course of the divine Pen: these are those who govern affairs. Among them are heavenly and earthly angels.” End of the abridged quotation. <span class=\"translator-note\"><strong>Source comparison:<\/strong> In the fuller passage of al-Bayḍāwī, <i>Anwār al-tanzīl<\/i>, I:67, on Q2:30, the view that angels are subtle bodies is attributed to most Muslims. He then introduces the philosophers’ account of angels as immaterial substances and places the twofold division under that account. Ibn ʿAjība’s abridgement, Cairo I:94–95, joins the subtle-bodies description directly to the two classes. The translation follows that abridgement; the fuller source distinguishes views whose transition has been omitted here. Abū al-Suʿūd, I:80, preserves the same distinction.<\/span><\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real Most High then disclosed the ground of Adam’s entitlement to vicegerency: his ennoblement through knowledge. “He taught Adam all the names,” that is, the things named. He cast into Adam’s heart the languages and letters, and the properties and benefits of things, that his descendants would require. He then displayed these named things to the angels, revealing their inability and honouring Adam through knowledge. He said: tell Me the names of these things, if you are truthful in your claim to deserve vicegerency. When they could not recognize those names, they replied, “Glory be to You”—we declare You free from purposeless action—“we have no knowledge except what You taught us. You are the Knowing,” of everything, “the Wise,” in Your perfect ordering of everything. This acknowledges their limitation and inability and indicates that their question was an inquiry seeking explanation of what they found difficult, not an objection. The Real, glorious is His majesty, said: “Adam, tell them their names,” specifying for them the name of each named thing. When he told them—for example, “This is a horse, and this a camel”—and distinguished these things for them, his excellence over them in knowledge became evident, establishing his entitlement to vicegerency. The Real Most High said: “Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and earth”—what is hidden—and know what you reveal in saying, “Will You place there…?” and what you conceal concerning your own entitlement to vicegerency, and your saying, “God will not create anyone more knowledgeable than us, since we came before”? Excellence belongs to the one who is true, not simply to the one who came first. Al-Bayḍāwī says: “Know that these verses indicate the dignity of the human being, the distinction of knowledge and its superiority to worship, and that knowledge is a condition of vicegerency—indeed, its principal foundation. They indicate that ‘teaching’ may be predicated of God, although He may not be called ‘a teacher’ ( المعلّم ), since that designation belongs particularly to someone who practises it as a profession; that languages are divinely instituted ( توقيفية ), taught by God through revelation; and that Adam, peace be upon him, is superior to these angels because he knows more than they do. The more knowledgeable is superior, according to His words, ‘Are those who know equal to those who do not know?’ [39:9]. They also indicate that God knows things before they occur.” End of the abridged quotation. [B030] In explaining the angels, he says: “They are subtle bodies ( أجسام لطيفة ) capable of assuming forms and are divided into two classes. One is wholly absorbed in knowing the Real and free from occupying itself with anything else: these are the exalted ones and the angels brought near. The other administers affairs from heaven to earth according to the established decree and the course of the divine Pen: these are those who govern affairs. Among them are heavenly and earthly angels.” End of the abridged quotation. Source comparison: In the fuller passage of al-Bayḍāwī, Anwār al-tanzīl , I:67, on Q2:30, the view that angels are subtle bodies is attributed to most Muslims. He then introduces the philosophers’ account of angels as immaterial substances and places the twofold division under that account. Ibn ʿAjība’s abridgement, Cairo I:94–95, joins the subtle-bodies description directly to the two classes. The translation follows that abridgement; the fuller source distinguishes views whose transition has been omitted here. Abū al-Suʿūd, I:80, preserves the same distinction."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"The human spirit and the disclosure of the names","html":"<p>Know that the spirit subsisting in this human being is a portion of the Supreme Spirit (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الروح الأعظم<\/bdi>), which is the meanings subsisting in the vessels (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المعاني القائمة بالأواني<\/bdi>). It is the Greater Adam and most ancient father. Concerning this Ibn al-Fāriḍ says:<\/p><blockquote class=\"poetry\">Though in form I am Adam’s son,<br>within him I have a meaning that witnesses to my fatherhood.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-35\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B031]<\/a><\/blockquote><p>When the Real Most High wished to appoint this spirit as vicegerent within human embodiment, to govern it and dispose of it as intended, the angels said through the tongue of their state (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بلسان حالها<\/bdi>): how can You place within it one who corrupts it by inclining to egoic shares and desires, and sheds blood through anger and partisan passions, while we glorify You and declare You free from what does not befit You? The angels saw some spirits incline to the lowest depth, but did not see the purification and ascent of others. The Real Most High told them, “I know what you do not know.” Among them are spirits that ascend to the Throne of the Presence, worship Me through contemplation and vision, embrace the whole of existence, and have the mysteries of the Essence, the lights of the attributes and the names of the named things unveiled to them.<\/p><p>The Real Most High says to the angels: has any of you had this concealed mystery and guarded Name unveiled to him? They reply, “Glory be to You! We have no knowledge except what You have taught us”—knowledge of the attributes, not the mysteries of the Essence—“You are the Knowing, the Wise.” The Real Most High says to the gnostic’s spirit, which has penetrated to the ocean of the Essence’s unity and the current of the attributes: acquaint them with what is hidden from them of the mysteries of the jabarūt and the names of the malakūt. When it informs them of the mysteries unveiled to it and the lights opened before it, they acknowledge the human being’s dignity and prostrate before Adam’s appearance, peace be upon him. The Real says to them: “Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and earth?”—the mysteries hidden in the heaven of spirits and the lights hidden in the earth of souls. I know the obedience you display and the belief you conceal. And God Most High knows best.<\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"Know that the spirit subsisting in this human being is a portion of the Supreme Spirit ( الروح الأعظم ), which is the meanings subsisting in the vessels ( المعاني القائمة بالأواني ). It is the Greater Adam and most ancient father. Concerning this Ibn al-Fāriḍ says: Though in form I am Adam’s son, within him I have a meaning that witnesses to my fatherhood. [B031] When the Real Most High wished to appoint this spirit as vicegerent within human embodiment, to govern it and dispose of it as intended, the angels said through the tongue of their state ( بلسان حالها ): how can You place within it one who corrupts it by inclining to egoic shares and desires, and sheds blood through anger and partisan passions, while we glorify You and declare You free from what does not befit You? The angels saw some spirits incline to the lowest depth, but did not see the purification and ascent of others. The Real Most High told them, “I know what you do not know.” Among them are spirits that ascend to the Throne of the Presence, worship Me through contemplation and vision, embrace the whole of existence, and have the mysteries of the Essence, the lights of the attributes and the names of the named things unveiled to them. The Real Most High says to the angels: has any of you had this concealed mystery and guarded Name unveiled to him? They reply, “Glory be to You! We have no knowledge except what You have taught us”—knowledge of the attributes, not the mysteries of the Essence—“You are the Knowing, the Wise.” The Real Most High says to the gnostic’s spirit, which has penetrated to the ocean of the Essence’s unity and the current of the attributes: acquaint them with what is hidden from them of the mysteries of the jabarūt and the names of the malakūt. When it informs them of the mysteries unveiled to it and the lights opened before it, they acknowledge the human being’s dignity and prostrate before Adam’s appearance, peace be upon him. The Real says to them: “Did I not tell you that I know the unseen of the heavens and earth?”—the mysteries hidden in the heaven of spirits and the lights hidden in the earth of souls. I know the obedience you display and the belief you conceal. And God Most High knows best."},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>Once Adam’s dignity was disclosed and his excellence became clear, He commanded them to prostrate before him, saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"Once Adam’s dignity was disclosed and his excellence became clear, He commanded them to prostrate before him, saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[],"english_characters":7309,"arabic_characters":4936},{"id":"q2-34","q":"2:34","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:34 · Prostration, pride and the distinction between sin and unbelief","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 95–96","cairo":"I:95–96","source_page_first":95,"source_page_last":96,"ar":"وَإِذْ قُلْنا لِلْمَلائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلاَّ إِبْلِيسَ أَبى وَاسْتَكْبَرَ وَكانَ مِنَ الْكافِرِينَ (34)\nقلت: (إذ) ظرف للماضي، ضد إذا، وهي معمولة لفعل مقدر، يفسره قوله تعالى: وَاذْكُرُوا إِذْ كُنْتُمْ، فحيثما وردت في القرآن فيقدر له «اذكر» ، والاستثناء متصل إذا قلنا إبليس من الملائكة، ومنقطع إذا قلنا من الجن. والله تعالى أعلم.\nيقول الحق جلّ جلاله: واذكر إِذْ قُلْنا لِلْمَلائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ، لما تبينت فضيلة، آدم أمرهم بالسجود، فقال لهم: اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ سجود انحناء، فَسَجَدُوا كلهم، لأنهم شهدوا الجمع ولم يشهدوا الفرق، فرأوا آدم قِبْلَةً، أو نوراً من أنوار عظمته، إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ أي: امتنع حيث نظر الفرق بحكمة الواحد القهار، فاستكبر وَكانَ من جملة الْكافِرِينَ. وكفره باعتراضه على الله وتسفيه حكمه، لا بامتناعه إذ مجرد المعصية لا تكفر. والله تعالى أعلم.\nالإشارة: إذا كمل تصفية الروح، وظهر شرفها، خضع لها كل شيء، وتواضع لها كل شيء، وانقاد لأمرها مَن سبقت له العناية، وهبت عليه ريح الهداية، لأنها صارت آدم الأكبر، إلا من إبلسته المشيئة، وطردته القدرة، فاستكبر عن تحكيم جنسه على نفسه، وكان من الكافرين لوجود الخصوصية، فجزاؤه حرمان شهود طلعة الربوبية، وهبوطه إلى حضيض العمومية.\nثم ذكر الحق تعالى دخول آدم الجنة، ونزوله إلى الخلافة التي أخبر الحق تعالى بها قبل، فقال:","quran_ar":"وَإِذْ قُلْنا لِلْمَلائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلاَّ إِبْلِيسَ أَبى وَاسْتَكْبَرَ وَكانَ مِنَ الْكافِرِينَ (34)","quran_en":"34. When We said to the angels, “Prostrate before Adam,” they prostrated, except Iblīs. He refused, grew proud, and was among the unbelievers.","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"The past-time particle and the exception","html":"<p>I say: <i>idh<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إذ<\/bdi>) is an adverbial expression for past time, the opposite of <i>idhā<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إذا<\/bdi>). It is governed by an implied verb, explained by His words “Remember when you were…”: wherever it occurs in the Qurʾān, “remember” is supplied. The exception (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الاستثناء<\/bdi>) is connected if we say Iblīs was one of the angels, and disconnected if we say he belonged to the jinn. And God Most High knows best.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-36\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B032]<\/a><\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"I say: idh ( إذ ) is an adverbial expression for past time, the opposite of idhā ( إذا ). It is governed by an implied verb, explained by His words “Remember when you were…”: wherever it occurs in the Qurʾān, “remember” is supplied. The exception ( الاستثناء ) is connected if we say Iblīs was one of the angels, and disconnected if we say he belonged to the jinn. And God Most High knows best. [B032]"},{"type":"theology","title":"The cause of Iblīs’s unbelief","html":"<p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when We told the angels to prostrate before Adam. Once Adam’s excellence was apparent, He commanded their prostration, telling them, “Prostrate before Adam,” with a prostration of bowing. They all prostrated because they witnessed gathering (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجمع<\/bdi>), not distinction (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفرق<\/bdi>): they saw Adam as a direction of prayer or a light among the lights of His greatness. Iblīs alone refused, looking to distinction, by the wisdom of the One, the All-Subduing. He grew proud and belonged among the unbelievers. His unbelief lay in objecting to God and declaring His judgement foolish, not simply in refusing, since bare disobedience does not constitute unbelief. And God Most High knows best.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: remember when We told the angels to prostrate before Adam. Once Adam’s excellence was apparent, He commanded their prostration, telling them, “Prostrate before Adam,” with a prostration of bowing. They all prostrated because they witnessed gathering ( الجمع ), not distinction ( الفرق ): they saw Adam as a direction of prayer or a light among the lights of His greatness. Iblīs alone refused, looking to distinction, by the wisdom of the One, the All-Subduing. He grew proud and belonged among the unbelievers. His unbelief lay in objecting to God and declaring His judgement foolish, not simply in refusing, since bare disobedience does not constitute unbelief. And God Most High knows best."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"A purified spirit and the refusal to submit","html":"<p>When the spirit’s purification is complete and its dignity becomes manifest, everything bows and humbles itself before it. Whoever has been embraced by antecedent providence and touched by the breeze of guidance submits to its command, for it has become the Greater Adam. The exception is one made an Iblīs by the divine will and driven away by power: he is too proud to submit himself to the judgement of another of his own kind, and becomes one of those who deny the existence of special election. His recompense is deprivation of witnessing the appearance of lordship and descent to the low ground of the ordinary condition.<\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"When the spirit’s purification is complete and its dignity becomes manifest, everything bows and humbles itself before it. Whoever has been embraced by antecedent providence and touched by the breeze of guidance submits to its command, for it has become the Greater Adam. The exception is one made an Iblīs by the divine will and driven away by power: he is too proud to submit himself to the judgement of another of his own kind, and becomes one of those who deny the existence of special election. His recompense is deprivation of witnessing the appearance of lordship and descent to the low ground of the ordinary condition."},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>The Real Most High then mentions Adam’s entry into Paradise and his descent to the vicegerency of which He had spoken earlier, saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real Most High then mentions Adam’s entry into Paradise and his descent to the vicegerency of which He had spoken earlier, saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[],"english_characters":1896,"arabic_characters":1195},{"id":"q2-35-37","q":"2:35–37","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:35–37 · Adam’s lapse, repentance and descent to vicegerency","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 96–97","cairo":"I:96–97","source_page_first":96,"source_page_last":97,"ar":"وَقُلْنا يا آدَمُ اسْكُنْ أَنْتَ وَزَوْجُكَ الْجَنَّةَ وَكُلا مِنْها رَغَداً حَيْثُ شِئْتُما وَلا تَقْرَبا هذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُونا مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ (35) فَأَزَلَّهُمَا الشَّيْطانُ عَنْها فَأَخْرَجَهُما مِمَّا كانا فِيهِ وَقُلْنَا اهْبِطُوا بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ وَلَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ مُسْتَقَرٌّ وَمَتاعٌ إِلى حِينٍ (36) فَتَلَقَّى آدَمُ مِنْ رَبِّهِ كَلِماتٍ فَتابَ عَلَيْهِ إِنَّهُ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ (37)\nقلت: (رغداً) : صفة لمصدر محذوف، أي: أكلا رغداً واسعاً، و (تكونا) : منصوب، جواب الأمر، أو معطوف على (تقرباً) ، و (أزلهما) : أوقعهما في الزلل بسبب الأكل، أو أذهبهما عن الجنة، ويدل عليه قراءة حمزة:\n«فأزالهما» ، وجملة (بعضكم لبعض عدو) : حالية، أي: متعادين.\nيقول الحق جلّ جلاله: وَقُلْنا يَا آدَمُ حين سجدت له الملائكة ودخل الجنة: اسْكُنْ أَنْتَ وَزَوْجُكَ حواء الْجَنَّةَ، وكانت خلقت من ضلعه الأيسر، وَكُلا من ثمار الجنة حَيْثُ شِئْتُما وَلا تَقْرَبا هذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ: العنب أو التين أو الحنطة فَتَكُونا إن أكلتما منها مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ لنفسيكما. فدخل إبليس خفية أو في فم الحية(1)، فتكلم مع آدم عليه السلام فقال له آدمُ عليه السلام: ما أحسن هذه الحالة لو كان الخلود. فحفظها إبليس، ووجد فيها مدخلاً من جهة الطمع، فقال له: هَلْ أَدُلُّكَ عَلى شَجَرَةِ الْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لاَّ يَبْلى فدلّه على أكل الشجرة، وقال: مَا نَهاكُما رَبُّكُما عنها إِلَّا كراهية أَنْ تَكُونا مَلَكَيْنِ أَوْ تَكُونا مِنَ\nالْخالِدِينَ وَقاسَمَهُما إِنِّي لَكُما لَمِنَ النَّاصِحِينَ. وأكلت حواء أولاً، ثم قالت له: قد أكلتُ ولم يضرني، ثم أكل آدم عليه السلام من جنس الشجرة، لا من عينها، متأوّلاً، فطار التاج واللباس، وأخرجهما مِمَّا كانا فِيهِ من رغد العيش والهناء، وأهبطهما إلى الأرض، للتعب والعناء، ليكون خليفة على ما سبق به القضاء.\nفقال لهم الحق تعالى: اهْبِطُوا آدم وحواء وإبليس والحية، بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ وَلَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ استقرار وتمتع إِلى حِينٍ وفاتكم، فتقدمون علي فيجازي المحسن بإحسانه، والمسيء بإساءته، فَتَلَقَّى أي أخذ آدَمُ مِنْ رَبِّهِ كَلِماتٍ وهي: رَبَّنا ظَلَمْنا أَنْفُسَنا وَإِنْ لَمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنا وَتَرْحَمْنا لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْخاسِرِينَ، فَتابَ الحق تعالى عليه واجتباه لحضرته، فإنه توّاب كثير التوبة على عباده، رحيم بهم، أرحم من أبيهم وأمهم، اللهم ارحمنا رحمة تعصمنا بها عن رؤية السّوي، إِنك على كل شيءٍ قدير.\nالإشارة: يقول الحق جلّ جلاله للروح، إذا كمل تهذيبها، وتمت تربيتها: اسكن أنت وبشريتك التي تزوجتها- قال تعالى: وَإِذَا النُّفُوسُ زُوِّجَتْ- جنة المعارف، وَكُلا من ثمار أذواقها وأنهار علومها، وتبوَّءًا من قصور ترقياتها، أكلاً واسعاً ما دمتما متحليين بالأدب، ولا تقربا شجرة المعصية وسوء الأدب (فتكونا من الظالمين) ، فلما سكنت جنة الخلود، وشَرهَتْ إلى الخلود، أهبطها الله إلى أرض العبودية، وردها إلى البقاء لتستحق الخلافة، وتقوم بحقوق الربوبية، بسبب ما ارتكبه من المعصية، وهي الشَّرهُ إلى دوام الحرية، «أكْرِمْ بها معصية أورثت الخلافة!» ، فكل ما ينزل بالروح إلى قهرية العبودية، فهو سبب إلى الترقي لشهود نور الربوبية، وربما قضى عليك بالذنب فكان سبب الوصول، فلما أراد الحق تعالى أن ينزلها إلى أرض العبودية بالسلوك بعد الجذب، قال لها ولمن يحاربها من الشيطان والهوى والدنيا وسائر الحظوظ: اهبطوا بعضكم لبعض عدو، ولكم- أيها العارفون بعد جهاد أعدائكم- في أرض العبودية، استقرار وتمتعٌ بتجليات أنوار الربوبية، إلى حين الملاقاة الحقيقية. فتلقت الروح من ربها كلمات الإنابة، وهبَّ عليها، نسيم الهداية، بما سبق لها من عين العناية، فتاب عليها، وقرَّبها إلى حضرة الشهود، ومعاينة طلعة الملك الودود، إنه تواب رحيم جواد كريم.\nثم كرّر الحق تعالى أمرهم بالهبوط، فقال:","quran_ar":"وَقُلْنا يا آدَمُ اسْكُنْ أَنْتَ وَزَوْجُكَ الْجَنَّةَ وَكُلا مِنْها رَغَداً حَيْثُ شِئْتُما وَلا تَقْرَبا هذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُونا مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ (35) فَأَزَلَّهُمَا الشَّيْطانُ عَنْها فَأَخْرَجَهُما مِمَّا كانا فِيهِ وَقُلْنَا اهْبِطُوا بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ وَلَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ مُسْتَقَرٌّ وَمَتاعٌ إِلى حِينٍ (36) فَتَلَقَّى آدَمُ مِنْ رَبِّهِ كَلِماتٍ فَتابَ عَلَيْهِ إِنَّهُ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ (37)","quran_en":"35. We said, “Adam, dwell with your spouse in the Garden, and eat freely from it wherever you wish; but do not approach this tree, lest you both become wrongdoers.” 36. Then Satan caused them to slip from it and brought them out of the state they had enjoyed. We said, “Go down, enemies to one another; on earth you shall have a dwelling-place and enjoyment for a time.” 37. Then Adam received words from his Lord, and He turned towards him in mercy. He is indeed the Ever-Relenting, the Merciful.","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"Abundant eating and the cause of the lapse","html":"<p>I say: “freely” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">رغداً<\/bdi>) qualifies an omitted verbal noun: “eat an abundant, ample eating.” “Become” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تكونا<\/bdi>) is subjunctive as the response to the injunction, or coordinated with “approach” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تقربا<\/bdi>). “He caused them to slip” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أزلهما<\/bdi>) means that he made them fall into error through eating, or removed them from the Garden. Ḥamza’s reading, “he removed them” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">فأزالهما<\/bdi>), supports the latter. “Enemies to one another” is a circumstantial clause: “being mutually hostile.”<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-37\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B033]<\/a><\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"I say: “freely” ( رغداً ) qualifies an omitted verbal noun: “eat an abundant, ample eating.” “Become” ( تكونا ) is subjunctive as the response to the injunction, or coordinated with “approach” ( تقربا ). “He caused them to slip” ( أزلهما ) means that he made them fall into error through eating, or removed them from the Garden. Ḥamza’s reading, “he removed them” ( فأزالهما ), supports the latter. “Enemies to one another” is a circumstantial clause: “being mutually hostile.” [B033]"},{"type":"exposition","title":"The temptation and the words of return","html":"<p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: after the angels prostrated before Adam and he entered the Garden, We said, “Adam, dwell with your spouse Eve in the Garden.” She had been created from his left rib. “Eat of the Garden’s fruits wherever you wish, but do not approach this tree”—the vine, fig, or wheat—“lest,” by eating from it, “you wrong yourselves.” Iblīs entered secretly or in the serpent’s mouth and spoke with Adam, peace be upon him. Adam said, “How excellent this state would be, were it everlasting!” Iblīs remembered this and found in covetousness an opening. He said, “Shall I lead you to the tree of everlasting life and a dominion that never decays?” [20:120]. He directed him to eat from the tree, saying: “Your Lord only forbade you it lest<\/p><p>you become two angels or become immortal”; and he swore to them, “I am a sincere adviser to you both” [7:20–21]. Eve ate first, then said, “I have eaten and it has not harmed me.” Adam then ate from the kind of tree, not the particular tree itself, acting on an interpretation. The crown and clothing flew away. Satan brought them out of the ease and happiness they had enjoyed, and they were sent down to earth, to toil and hardship, so that Adam might become vicegerent according to the antecedent decree.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-38\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B034]<\/a><\/p><p>The Real Most High told them—Adam, Eve, Iblīs and the serpent—“Go down, enemies to one another. On earth you shall have residence and enjoyment until your deaths; then you come before Me, and the doer of good is recompensed for his goodness and the evildoer for his wrongdoing.” Adam received, that is, took, words from his Lord: “Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves. If You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we shall surely be among the losers” [7:23]. The Real Most High turned towards him and chose him for His Presence, for He continually turns towards His servants and is merciful to them, more merciful than their fathers and mothers. God, grant us a mercy that protects us from seeing other-than-You: You have power over all things.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: after the angels prostrated before Adam and he entered the Garden, We said, “Adam, dwell with your spouse Eve in the Garden.” She had been created from his left rib. “Eat of the Garden’s fruits wherever you wish, but do not approach this tree”—the vine, fig, or wheat—“lest,” by eating from it, “you wrong yourselves.” Iblīs entered secretly or in the serpent’s mouth and spoke with Adam, peace be upon him. Adam said, “How excellent this state would be, were it everlasting!” Iblīs remembered this and found in covetousness an opening. He said, “Shall I lead you to the tree of everlasting life and a dominion that never decays?” [20:120]. He directed him to eat from the tree, saying: “Your Lord only forbade you it lest you become two angels or become immortal”; and he swore to them, “I am a sincere adviser to you both” [7:20–21]. Eve ate first, then said, “I have eaten and it has not harmed me.” Adam then ate from the kind of tree, not the particular tree itself, acting on an interpretation. The crown and clothing flew away. Satan brought them out of the ease and happiness they had enjoyed, and they were sent down to earth, to toil and hardship, so that Adam might become vicegerent according to the antecedent decree. [B034] The Real Most High told them—Adam, Eve, Iblīs and the serpent—“Go down, enemies to one another. On earth you shall have residence and enjoyment until your deaths; then you come before Me, and the doer of good is recompensed for his goodness and the evildoer for his wrongdoing.” Adam received, that is, took, words from his Lord: “Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves. If You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we shall surely be among the losers” [7:23]. The Real Most High turned towards him and chose him for His Presence, for He continually turns towards His servants and is merciful to them, more merciful than their fathers and mothers. God, grant us a mercy that protects us from seeing other-than-You: You have power over all things."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"The return from attraction to servanthood","html":"<p>When the spirit’s refinement is complete and its formation perfected, the Real, glorious is His majesty, tells it: dwell, with the human embodiment you have married—He says, “When souls are paired” [81:7]—in the garden of gnosis. Eat of the fruits of its spiritual tastings and the rivers of its sciences, and take up residence in the palaces of its ascents, eating freely so long as you remain adorned with courtesy. Do not approach the tree of disobedience and ill courtesy, lest you become wrongdoers.<\/p><p>When it dwelt in the garden of permanence and greedily desired to remain there, God sent it down to the earth of servanthood and returned it to subsistence (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">البقاء<\/bdi>), so that it might deserve vicegerency and fulfil the claims of lordship, through the disobedience it committed: greedy desire for perpetual freedom. “How noble a disobedience that bequeathed vicegerency!” Everything that brings the spirit down into the compelling condition of servanthood becomes a means of ascent to witnessing the light of lordship. He may decree a sin for you, and it becomes the means of arrival.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-39\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B035]<\/a><\/p><p>When the Real Most High wished to bring it down to the earth of servanthood through wayfaring after attraction (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">السلوك بعد الجذب<\/bdi>), He told it and its adversaries—Satan, caprice, the world and the other egoic shares—“Go down, enemies to one another.” After striving against your enemies, you gnostics have in the earth of servanthood a dwelling and enjoyment of the self-disclosures of the lights of lordship until the true meeting. The spirit receives from its Lord words of turning back. The breeze of guidance blows over it through the providence already bestowed upon it; He turns towards it and brings it near to the presence of witnessing and the direct vision of the loving King’s appearance. He is the Ever-Relenting, Merciful, Munificent, Generous.<\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"When the spirit’s refinement is complete and its formation perfected, the Real, glorious is His majesty, tells it: dwell, with the human embodiment you have married—He says, “When souls are paired” [81:7]—in the garden of gnosis. Eat of the fruits of its spiritual tastings and the rivers of its sciences, and take up residence in the palaces of its ascents, eating freely so long as you remain adorned with courtesy. Do not approach the tree of disobedience and ill courtesy, lest you become wrongdoers. When it dwelt in the garden of permanence and greedily desired to remain there, God sent it down to the earth of servanthood and returned it to subsistence ( البقاء ), so that it might deserve vicegerency and fulfil the claims of lordship, through the disobedience it committed: greedy desire for perpetual freedom. “How noble a disobedience that bequeathed vicegerency!” Everything that brings the spirit down into the compelling condition of servanthood becomes a means of ascent to witnessing the light of lordship. He may decree a sin for you, and it becomes the means of arrival. [B035] When the Real Most High wished to bring it down to the earth of servanthood through wayfaring after attraction ( السلوك بعد الجذب ), He told it and its adversaries—Satan, caprice, the world and the other egoic shares—“Go down, enemies to one another.” After striving against your enemies, you gnostics have in the earth of servanthood a dwelling and enjoyment of the self-disclosures of the lights of lordship until the true meeting. The spirit receives from its Lord words of turning back. The breeze of guidance blows over it through the providence already bestowed upon it; He turns towards it and brings it near to the presence of witnessing and the direct vision of the loving King’s appearance. He is the Ever-Relenting, Merciful, Munificent, Generous."},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>The Real Most High repeats His command that they descend, saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real Most High repeats His command that they descend, saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[{"id":"C96.1","page":96,"ar":"ليس لنا البحث عن كيفية وسوسة إبليس لآدم، ولا نقطع القول بلا دليل. وهذا من الإنصاف.","en":"It is not for us to investigate how Iblīs whispered to Adam, nor to state a conclusion decisively without evidence. This is a matter of fairness.","anchor":"فدخل إبليس خفية أو في فم الحية"}],"english_characters":4428,"arabic_characters":3289},{"id":"q2-38-39","q":"2:38–39","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:38–39 · Guidance after descent and the inseparability of law and realization","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 97–99","cairo":"I:97–99","source_page_first":97,"source_page_last":99,"ar":"قُلْنَا اهْبِطُوا مِنْها جَمِيعاً فَإِمَّا يَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِنِّي هُدىً فَمَنْ تَبِعَ هُدايَ فَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (38) وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَكَذَّبُوا بِآياتِنا أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (39)\nقلت: (إن) : شرط، و (ما) زيدت لتقوية الشرط، ولذلك دخلت نون التوكيد، وعبر بإن دون (إذا) ، مع تحقق مجيئ الهدى لأنه غير واجب عقلاً، وجملة الشرط الثاني وجوابه، الشرط الأول، و (جميعاً) حال مؤكدة أي:\nاهبطوا أنتم أجمعون، ولذلك لا يقتضى اجتماعهم على الهبوط في زمان واحد.\nولما أمر الحقّ جلا جلاله آدم أولاً بالهبوط من الجنة، جعل يبكي ويتضرّع ويقول: ألم تخلقني بيدك؟ ألم تسجد لي ملائكتك؟ ألم تدخلني جنتك؟ ثم ألهم الكلمات التي تلقاها من ربه، فتاب عليه ورحمه، فطمع آدم حين سمع من ربه قبول توبته في البقاء في الجنة، فقال له الحق جلّ جلاله: يا آدم لا يجاورني من عصاني، وقد سبقت كلمتي بهبوطك إلى الأرض لتكون خليفتي بذريتك، فكرّر عليه الأمر بالهبوط ثانياً. فقال: اهْبِطُوا مِنْها جَمِيعاً أنتما بما اشتملتما عليه من ذريتكما. فمهما يَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِنِّي هُدىً أي: بيان وإرشاد إلى توحيدي ومعرفتي، على يد رسول أو نائب عنه، فَمَنْ تَبِعَ ذلك الإرشاد، واهتدى إلى معرفتي وتوحيدي، وعمل بطاعتي وتكاليفي، فَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ من لحوق مكروه وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ من فوات محبوب، لأني أَصرف عنهم جميع المكاره، وأجلب لهم المنافع، وَالَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوا بِآياتِنا الدالة على قدرتنا المنزلة على رسلنا، واستكبروا عن النظر فيها، أو عن الخضوع لمن جاء بها، أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ.\nالإشارة: إذا سكنت الأرواح في عُشِّ الحضرة، وتمكنت من الشهود والنظرة، أمرها الحق تعالى بالنزول إلى سماء الحقوق أو أرض الحظوظ، فتنزل بالإذن والتمكين، والرسوخ في اليقين، لا لطلب جزاء أو لقضاء شهوة، بل تنزل بالله ومن الله وإلى الله، فمن نزل منها على هذا الهدى الحسن فَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ، ومن ركب بحر التوحيد مع غير رئيس عارف، ولم يأوِ إلى سفينة الشريعة، واستكبر عن الخضوع إلى تكاليفها لعبت به الأمواج، فكان من المغرقين. أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ لأن مَن تحقق ولم يتشرّع فقد تزندق، ومن تشرع ولم يتصوف فقد تفسّق، ومَن جمع بينهما فقد تحقق، جعلنا الله ممن تحقّق بهما. وسلك على منهاجهما إلى الممات، آمين.\nولما ذكر الحق تعالى شرف كتابه، ونفى وجود الريب عن ساحته، ثم دعا إلى توحيده، وبرهن على وجوده، بابتداء خلق العالم من عرشه إلى فرشه، وذكر كيفية ابتداء عمارته، خاطب بني إسرائيل لأنهم أهل العلم بالأخبار المتقدمة، وقد سمعوا هذه الأخبار من نَبِي أُمِّي لم يُعْهَدْ بقراءةٍ ولا تعلم، فقامت الحجة عليهم، وتحققوا أنه من عند الله. وما منعهم من الإسلام إلا الحسد وحب الرئاسة، فلذلك أطال الحق الكلام معهم، تارةً يُقرِّعَهم على عدم\nالإيمان وما فعلوا مع أنبيائهم، وتارة يذكرهم النِعَم التي أنعم الله على أسلافهم، فقال تعالى:","quran_ar":"قُلْنَا اهْبِطُوا مِنْها جَمِيعاً فَإِمَّا يَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِنِّي هُدىً فَمَنْ تَبِعَ هُدايَ فَلا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (38) وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَكَذَّبُوا بِآياتِنا أُولئِكَ أَصْحابُ النَّارِ هُمْ فِيها خالِدُونَ (39)","quran_en":"38. We said, “Go down from it, all of you. Whenever guidance comes to you from Me, those who follow My guidance shall have no fear, nor shall they grieve. 39. But those who disbelieve and deny Our signs are the companions of the Fire; there they shall abide.”","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"The condition and the gift of guidance","html":"<p>I say: <i>in<\/i> (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إن<\/bdi>) is conditional; <i>mā<\/i> is added to strengthen the condition, and for this reason the emphatic nūn enters the verb. <i>In<\/i>, rather than <i>idhā<\/i>, is used although the coming of guidance is certain, because it is not rationally obligatory. The second conditional sentence, with its response, supplies the response to the first condition. “All together” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">جميعاً<\/bdi>) is an emphatic circumstantial expression: “descend, every one of you.” It therefore does not require their descending at one and the same time.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-40\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B036]<\/a><\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"I say: in ( إن ) is conditional; mā is added to strengthen the condition, and for this reason the emphatic nūn enters the verb. In , rather than idhā , is used although the coming of guidance is certain, because it is not rationally obligatory. The second conditional sentence, with its response, supplies the response to the first condition. “All together” ( جميعاً ) is an emphatic circumstantial expression: “descend, every one of you.” It therefore does not require their descending at one and the same time. [B036]"},{"type":"exposition","title":"Repentance does not annul the appointed vicegerency","html":"<p>When the Real, glorious is His majesty, first commanded Adam to leave the Garden, he wept and implored: “Did You not create me with Your hand? Did You not make Your angels prostrate before me? Did You not admit me to Your Garden?” He was then inspired with the words he received from his Lord, who turned towards him and had mercy on him. Hearing that his repentance had been accepted, Adam hoped to remain in the Garden. The Real, glorious is His majesty, told him: “Adam, one who has disobeyed Me does not remain My neighbour. My word has already gone forth that you descend to earth to be My vicegerent through your offspring.” He therefore repeated the command to descend: “Go down from it, all of you”—the two of you together with the offspring contained in you.<\/p><p>Whenever guidance comes to you from Me—explanation and direction towards affirming My unity and knowing Me, at the hands of a messenger or his deputy—whoever follows that direction, is guided to My knowledge and unity, and observes My obedience and obligations shall have no fear of harm overtaking him or grief over losing something beloved. I turn every harm away from them and bring benefits to them. Those who deny Our signs, which demonstrate Our power and are sent down upon Our messengers, and are too proud to consider them or submit to their bearer, are the companions of the Fire; there they abide for ever.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"When the Real, glorious is His majesty, first commanded Adam to leave the Garden, he wept and implored: “Did You not create me with Your hand? Did You not make Your angels prostrate before me? Did You not admit me to Your Garden?” He was then inspired with the words he received from his Lord, who turned towards him and had mercy on him. Hearing that his repentance had been accepted, Adam hoped to remain in the Garden. The Real, glorious is His majesty, told him: “Adam, one who has disobeyed Me does not remain My neighbour. My word has already gone forth that you descend to earth to be My vicegerent through your offspring.” He therefore repeated the command to descend: “Go down from it, all of you”—the two of you together with the offspring contained in you. Whenever guidance comes to you from Me—explanation and direction towards affirming My unity and knowing Me, at the hands of a messenger or his deputy—whoever follows that direction, is guided to My knowledge and unity, and observes My obedience and obligations shall have no fear of harm overtaking him or grief over losing something beloved. I turn every harm away from them and bring benefits to them. Those who deny Our signs, which demonstrate Our power and are sent down upon Our messengers, and are too proud to consider them or submit to their bearer, are the companions of the Fire; there they abide for ever."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"Descending with permission and remaining in the ship of the Law","html":"<p>When spirits dwell in the nest of the Presence and become established in witnessing and vision, the Real Most High commands them to descend to the heaven of rightful obligations or the earth of allotted enjoyments (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">سماء الحقوق أو أرض الحظوظ<\/bdi>). They descend by permission and firm establishment, rooted in certainty—not to seek recompense or gratify desire. Rather, they descend by God, from God and unto God. Those who descend upon this beautiful guidance have no fear and do not grieve.<\/p><p>But whoever sails the ocean of unity without a knowing captain, does not take refuge in the ship of the Sacred Law, and is too proud to submit to its obligations is tossed by the waves and drowned. Such are the companions of the Fire, abiding therein. For whoever pursues realization without observing the Law falls into heresy; whoever observes the Law without Sufi purification falls into transgression; and whoever unites the two attains realization. May God make us among those who realize both and follow their way until death. Amen.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-41\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B037]<\/a><\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"When spirits dwell in the nest of the Presence and become established in witnessing and vision, the Real Most High commands them to descend to the heaven of rightful obligations or the earth of allotted enjoyments ( سماء الحقوق أو أرض الحظوظ ). They descend by permission and firm establishment, rooted in certainty—not to seek recompense or gratify desire. Rather, they descend by God, from God and unto God. Those who descend upon this beautiful guidance have no fear and do not grieve. But whoever sails the ocean of unity without a knowing captain, does not take refuge in the ship of the Sacred Law, and is too proud to submit to its obligations is tossed by the waves and drowned. Such are the companions of the Fire, abiding therein. For whoever pursues realization without observing the Law falls into heresy; whoever observes the Law without Sufi purification falls into transgression; and whoever unites the two attains realization. May God make us among those who realize both and follow their way until death. Amen. [B037]"},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>Having declared His Book’s dignity and excluded doubt from its precincts, then summoned people to His unity and demonstrated His existence through the beginning of the world’s creation, from its throne to its carpet, and described how it first became inhabited, the Real Most High addresses the Children of Israel. They possess knowledge of the earlier accounts and have heard these accounts from an unlettered Prophet not known for reading or instruction. The proof has therefore been established against them, and they recognize that it comes from God. Nothing prevents their embracing Islam but envy and love of leadership. For this reason the Real speaks to them at length: sometimes rebuking their failure<\/p><p>to believe and their treatment of their prophets, sometimes reminding them of the blessings He bestowed upon their forebears. He says:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"Having declared His Book’s dignity and excluded doubt from its precincts, then summoned people to His unity and demonstrated His existence through the beginning of the world’s creation, from its throne to its carpet, and described how it first became inhabited, the Real Most High addresses the Children of Israel. They possess knowledge of the earlier accounts and have heard these accounts from an unlettered Prophet not known for reading or instruction. The proof has therefore been established against them, and they recognize that it comes from God. Nothing prevents their embracing Islam but envy and love of leadership. For this reason the Real speaks to them at length: sometimes rebuking their failure to believe and their treatment of their prophets, sometimes reminding them of the blessings He bestowed upon their forebears. He says:"}],"cairo_notes":[],"english_characters":3783,"arabic_characters":2562},{"id":"q2-40-43","q":"2:40–43","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:40–43 · Remembering blessings and fulfilling the covenant","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 99–100","cairo":"I:99–100","source_page_first":99,"source_page_last":100,"ar":"يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَوْفُوا بِعَهْدِي أُوفِ بِعَهْدِكُمْ وَإِيَّايَ فَارْهَبُونِ (40) وَآمِنُوا بِما أَنْزَلْتُ مُصَدِّقاً لِما مَعَكُمْ وَلا تَكُونُوا أَوَّلَ كافِرٍ بِهِ وَلا تَشْتَرُوا بِآياتِي ثَمَناً قَلِيلاً وَإِيَّايَ فَاتَّقُونِ (41) وَلا تَلْبِسُوا الْحَقَّ بِالْباطِلِ وَتَكْتُمُوا الْحَقَّ وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ (42) وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكاةَ وَارْكَعُوا مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ (43)\nقلت: (إسرائيل) : هو يعقوب بن إسحاق بن إبراهيم الخليل- عليهم الصلاة والسلام- وهو اسم عجمي، وبنو تميم تقول: «إسرائين» بالنون، (وإسرا) بالعبرانية: عبد، و (إيل) : اسم الله تعالى، فمعناه: عبد الله، وبنو إسرائيل:\nهم أولاد يعقوب عليه السلام، و (بعهدي) من إضافة المصدر إلى فاعله، وبِعَهْدِكُمْ إلى مفعوله، و (إياي) منصوب بفعل مضمر، يُقدر مؤخراً. أي: أياي ارهبوا فارهبون. وحذف مفعول (ارهبون) لرءوس الآي، وكذا قوله: (وإياي فاتقون) ، والرهبة: خوف مع تحرُّز، و (تكتموا) : معطوف على (تلبسوا) ، أو منصوب بأن مضمرة بعد النهي، و (أنتم تعلمون) : جملة حالية.\nيقول الحق جلّ جلاله: يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ التي خصصتُكم بها، بأن فضلتكم على أهل زمانكم، وجعلت فيكم أنبياء ورسلاً، كلما انقرض نبيّ بعثت نبيّاً آخر، وجعلتكم ملوكاً وحكاماً على الناس، قبل أن تفسدوا في الأرض بقتل الأنبياء، فتكفروا بهذه النعم، فإن الإنسان حسود غيور بالطبع، فإذا نظر إلى ما أنعم الله على غيره حمله الحسد والغيرة على السخط والكفران، وإذا نظر إلى ما أنعم الله به عليه حمله حب النعمة على الرضا والشكر. فاذكروا ما أنعمتُ به عليكم، وقيدوه بالشكر، وَأَوْفُوا بِعَهْدِي الذي عهدت إليكم، وهو أنكم إن أدركتم محمدا صلى الله عليه وسلّم لتؤمنن به ولتنصرنه، ولتبينن صفته التي في كتابكم، ولا تكتمونها، أُوفِ بِعَهْدِكُمْ بأن أدخلكم جنتي، وأبيح لكم النظر إلى وجهي، وأحل عليكم رضواني في جملة عبادي، ولا ترهبوا أحداً غيري، فإنه لا فاعل غيري.\nوبادروا إلى الإيمان بِما أَنْزَلْتُ على محمد رسولي، من كتابي، الذي هو مصدق لِما مَعَكُمْ من التوراة، ومهيمن عليه، وَلا تَكُونُوا أَوَّلَ فريق كافِرٍ بِهِ، فتبوءوا بإثمكم وإثم من تبعكم، ولا تستبدلوا الإيمان الذي هو سبب الفوز في الدارين، بالعرضِ الفاني الذي تأخذونه من سفلتكم، فإنه ثمن قليل يعقبه عذاب جليل وخزي كبير. ولا تخشوا أحداً سواي فإن النفع والضرر بيدي، ولا تخلطوا الْحَقَّ الذي هو ذكر\nمحمد صلى الله عليه وسلّم وصفته التي في كتابكم، بِالْباطِلِ الذي تريدونه تحريفاً وتأويلا، وَلا تَكْتُمُوا الْحَقَّ الذي عندكم من ذكر محمد وصحة رسالته، وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ أنكم محرفون، ولابسون عناداً وحسداً، فيحل عليكم غضبي وعقابي، وَمَنْ يَحْلِلْ عَلَيْهِ غَضَبِي فَقَدْ هَوى. فإذا حصلتم أصول الدين، وهو الإيمان، فاشتغلوا بفروعه، وهي الصلاة والزكاة وغيرهما، فأدوهما على منهاج المسلمين. واجعلوا صلاتكم في جماعة المؤمنين فإنَّ صلاة الجماعة تُفضلُ غيرها بسبعٍ وعشرين درجة، مع سريان الأسرار واقتباس الأنوار من الصالحين والأبرار، وبالله التوفيق.\nالإشارة: إذا توجَّه الخطاب إلى طائفة مخصوصة، حمله أهل الفهم عن الله على عمومه لكل سامع، فإن الملك إذا عاتب قوماً بمحضر آخرين، كان المراد بذلك تحذير كل مَن يسمع، فكأن الحق جل جلاله يقول: يا بني آدم اذكروا نعمتي التي أنعمت عليكم، وتفكروا في أصولها وفروعها، واشكروني عليها بنسبتها إليَّ وحدي، فإنه لا منعم غيري، فمن شكرني شكرته، ومن فيض إحساني وبري مددته، ومن كفر نعمتي سلبته، وعن بابي طردته، وأوفوا بعهدي بالقيام بوظائف العبودية، أوف بعهدكم بأن أطلعكم على أسرار الربوبية.\nأو: أوفوا بعهدي بالقيام برسوم الشريعة، أوفِ بعهدكم بالهداية إلى منار الطريقة، أو: أوفوا بعهدي بسلوك منهاج الطريقة، أوفِ بعهدكم بالإيصال إلى عين الحقيقة، أو: أوفوا بعهدي بالاستغراق في بحر الشهود، أوفِ بعهدكم بالترقي أبدا إلى الملك الودود، وخصّوني بالرهب والرغب، وتوجهوا إليّ في كل سؤال وطلب، أعطف عليكم بعنايتي وودي، وأمنحكم من عظيم إحساني ورفدي، وآمنوا بما أنزلت على قلوب أوليائى، من مواهب أسراري وآلائي، تصديقاً لما أتحفت به رسلي وأنبيائي، فكل ما ظهر على الأولياء فهو معجزة للأنبياء وتصديق لهم، ولا تبادروا بالإنكار على أوليائي، فتكونوا سبباً في طرد عبادي عن بابي، ولا يمنعكم حب الرئاسة والجاه عن الخضوع إلى أوليائي، ولا ترقبوا أحداً غيري، فإني أمنعكم من شهود سري.\nولا تلبسوا الحق بالباطل، فتظهروا شعار الصالحين وتبطنوا أخلاق الفاسقين، تتزيوا بزى الأولياء، وتفعلوا فعل الأغوياء، وإذا تحققتم بخصوصية أحد من عبادي، فلا تكتموها عن أهل محبتي وودادي، وأقيموا صلاة القلوب بالخضوع تحت مجاري الأقدار، وأدّوا زكاة النفوس بالذل والانكسار، وكونوا مع الخاشعين، واركعوا مع الراكعين، أمنحكم معونتي ونصري، وأفيض عليكم من بحر إحساني وبري، أنا عند المنكسرة قلوبُهم من أجلى.\nثم وبّخ الحق تعالى من عرف الحق وحرم نفسه منه من أهل الكتاب وغيرهم، فقال:","quran_ar":"يا بَنِي إِسْرائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَوْفُوا بِعَهْدِي أُوفِ بِعَهْدِكُمْ وَإِيَّايَ فَارْهَبُونِ (40) وَآمِنُوا بِما أَنْزَلْتُ مُصَدِّقاً لِما مَعَكُمْ وَلا تَكُونُوا أَوَّلَ كافِرٍ بِهِ وَلا تَشْتَرُوا بِآياتِي ثَمَناً قَلِيلاً وَإِيَّايَ فَاتَّقُونِ (41) وَلا تَلْبِسُوا الْحَقَّ بِالْباطِلِ وَتَكْتُمُوا الْحَقَّ وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ (42) وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكاةَ وَارْكَعُوا مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ (43)","quran_en":"40. Children of Israel, remember My blessing which I bestowed upon you. Fulfil My covenant, and I shall fulfil your covenant; and fear Me alone. 41. Believe in what I have sent down, confirming what is with you; do not be the first to disbelieve in it. Do not sell My signs for a paltry price, and be mindful of Me alone. 42. Do not clothe truth in falsehood or conceal the truth while you know. 43. Establish prayer, give the purifying alms, and bow with those who bow.","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"Israel, the covenant and the fronted pronoun","html":"<p>I say: Israel is Jacob, son of Isaac, son of Abraham the Friend, peace and blessings be upon them. It is a non-Arabic name; the Banū Tamīm pronounce it <i>Isrāʾīn<\/i>, with nūn. In Hebrew, <i>isrā<\/i> means servant and <i>īl<\/i> is a name of God Most High, so its meaning is “servant of God.” The Children of Israel are Jacob’s descendants.<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-42\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B038]<\/a><\/p><p>“My covenant” is an annexation of the verbal noun to its agent (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إضافة المصدر إلى فاعله<\/bdi>), while “your covenant” annexes it to its object. “Me alone” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إياي<\/bdi>) is accusative through an implied verb, reconstructed after it: “Me fear—so fear Me.” The object of “fear Me” is omitted for the verse-endings, as also in “be mindful of Me alone.” Fear (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الرهبة<\/bdi>) here is fear accompanied by self-guarding. “Conceal” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تكتموا<\/bdi>) is coordinated with “clothe” (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تلبسوا<\/bdi>), or subjunctive through an implicit <i>an<\/i> after the prohibition. “While you know” is circumstantial.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"I say: Israel is Jacob, son of Isaac, son of Abraham the Friend, peace and blessings be upon them. It is a non-Arabic name; the Banū Tamīm pronounce it Isrāʾīn , with nūn. In Hebrew, isrā means servant and īl is a name of God Most High, so its meaning is “servant of God.” The Children of Israel are Jacob’s descendants. [B038] “My covenant” is an annexation of the verbal noun to its agent ( إضافة المصدر إلى فاعله ), while “your covenant” annexes it to its object. “Me alone” ( إياي ) is accusative through an implied verb, reconstructed after it: “Me fear—so fear Me.” The object of “fear Me” is omitted for the verse-endings, as also in “be mindful of Me alone.” Fear ( الرهبة ) here is fear accompanied by self-guarding. “Conceal” ( تكتموا ) is coordinated with “clothe” ( تلبسوا ), or subjunctive through an implicit an after the prohibition. “While you know” is circumstantial."},{"type":"exposition","title":"Gratitude, truthfulness and worship","html":"<p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember the blessing with which I distinguished you: I preferred you over the people of your time and appointed prophets and messengers among you; whenever a prophet passed away, I sent another. I made you kings and governors over people before you corrupted the earth by killing the prophets and denied these blessings. Human beings are naturally prone to envy and rivalry: looking at what God gives another inclines them to resentment and ingratitude, whereas looking at what He gives them inclines them, through love of the blessing, to contentment and thanks. Remember My benefactions and secure them with gratitude.<\/p><p>Fulfil the covenant I made with you: should you live to encounter Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, you must believe in him, support him, and disclose rather than hide the description of him in your Book. I shall fulfil My covenant with you by admitting you to My Garden, permitting you to behold My Face, and bestowing My good pleasure upon you among My servants. Fear none but Me, for there is no agent other than Me.<\/p><p>Hasten to believe in My Book sent down upon My Messenger Muḥammad, confirming the Torah you possess and standing as its guardian. Do not be the first group to disbelieve in it, bearing both your own sin and that of your followers. Do not exchange faith—the means of success in both abodes—for the passing worldly gain you take from your lower ranks. It is a paltry price followed by mighty punishment and great disgrace. Fear none but Me, for benefit and harm are in My hand. Do not mix the truth—the mention<\/p><p>of Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, and his description in your Book—with the falsehood you intend through distortion and tendentious interpretation. Do not conceal the truth you possess about Muḥammad and the soundness of his mission, knowing that you distort and confuse through obstinacy and envy, lest My wrath and punishment fall upon you: “He upon whom My wrath falls has indeed fallen” [20:81].<\/p><p>Once you possess the foundations of religion—faith—occupy yourselves with its branches: prayer, almsgiving and the rest. Perform them according to the Muslims’ way and join the believers in congregational prayer. Congregational prayer surpasses other prayer by twenty-seven degrees, together with the circulation of spiritual mysteries and the receiving of lights from the righteous and good. Through God is success.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Israel, remember the blessing with which I distinguished you: I preferred you over the people of your time and appointed prophets and messengers among you; whenever a prophet passed away, I sent another. I made you kings and governors over people before you corrupted the earth by killing the prophets and denied these blessings. Human beings are naturally prone to envy and rivalry: looking at what God gives another inclines them to resentment and ingratitude, whereas looking at what He gives them inclines them, through love of the blessing, to contentment and thanks. Remember My benefactions and secure them with gratitude. Fulfil the covenant I made with you: should you live to encounter Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, you must believe in him, support him, and disclose rather than hide the description of him in your Book. I shall fulfil My covenant with you by admitting you to My Garden, permitting you to behold My Face, and bestowing My good pleasure upon you among My servants. Fear none but Me, for there is no agent other than Me. Hasten to believe in My Book sent down upon My Messenger Muḥammad, confirming the Torah you possess and standing as its guardian. Do not be the first group to disbelieve in it, bearing both your own sin and that of your followers. Do not exchange faith—the means of success in both abodes—for the passing worldly gain you take from your lower ranks. It is a paltry price followed by mighty punishment and great disgrace. Fear none but Me, for benefit and harm are in My hand. Do not mix the truth—the mention of Muḥammad, God bless him and grant him peace, and his description in your Book—with the falsehood you intend through distortion and tendentious interpretation. Do not conceal the truth you possess about Muḥammad and the soundness of his mission, knowing that you distort and confuse through obstinacy and envy, lest My wrath and punishment fall upon you: “He upon whom My wrath falls has indeed fallen” [20:81]. Once you possess the foundations of religion—faith—occupy yourselves with its branches: prayer, almsgiving and the rest. Perform them according to the Muslims’ way and join the believers in congregational prayer. Congregational prayer surpasses other prayer by twenty-seven degrees, together with the circulation of spiritual mysteries and the receiving of lights from the righteous and good. Through God is success."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"The successive fulfilments of the covenant","html":"<p>When an address is directed to a particular group, those who understand from God take its meaning as general for every hearer. When a king reproaches one people before others, his purpose is to warn everyone who hears. It is as though the Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Adam, remember My blessing upon you; reflect on its roots and branches, and thank Me by attributing it to Me alone, for none bestows blessings but I. Whoever thanks Me, I thank and sustain from the overflow of My kindness and beneficence. Whoever denies My blessing, I deprive and drive from My door.<\/p><p>Fulfil My covenant by discharging the duties of servanthood, and I fulfil yours by disclosing to you the mysteries of lordship. Or: fulfil My covenant by observing the forms of the Sacred Law, and I fulfil yours by guiding you to the beacon of the Path. Or: fulfil My covenant by travelling the Path, and I fulfil yours by bringing you to the very reality. Or: fulfil My covenant by immersion in the ocean of witnessing, and I fulfil yours through unceasing ascent towards the loving King. Direct fear and desire to Me alone, turning to Me in every request and need. I embrace you with My care and love and grant you immense beneficence and support.<\/p><p>Believe in the gifts of My mysteries and blessings that I send down upon My friends’ hearts, confirming what I bestowed on My messengers and prophets. Everything that appears upon the friends of God is a miracle of the prophets and a confirmation of them. Do not hasten to deny My friends and so become the cause of driving My servants from My door. Do not let love of leadership and rank prevent your submission to My friends; do not watch for another besides Me, lest I withhold from you the witnessing of My mystery.<\/p><p>Do not clothe truth in falsehood, displaying the marks of the righteous while concealing the character of transgressors, wearing the garb of God’s friends while acting as the misguided do. Once you recognize special election in one of My servants, do not hide it from the people of My love and affection. Establish the prayer of hearts by submission beneath the unfolding decrees; render the alms of souls through humility and brokenness. Be with the humble and bow with those who bow: I grant you My aid and victory and pour upon you from the ocean of My kindness and goodness. “I am with those whose hearts are broken for My sake.”<a class=\"source-marker\" href=\"Source_Reference_Ledger_XII.html#LEGACY-43\" title=\"Inherited reference occurrence; see current source status\">[B039]<\/a><\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"When an address is directed to a particular group, those who understand from God take its meaning as general for every hearer. When a king reproaches one people before others, his purpose is to warn everyone who hears. It is as though the Real, glorious is His majesty, says: Children of Adam, remember My blessing upon you; reflect on its roots and branches, and thank Me by attributing it to Me alone, for none bestows blessings but I. Whoever thanks Me, I thank and sustain from the overflow of My kindness and beneficence. Whoever denies My blessing, I deprive and drive from My door. Fulfil My covenant by discharging the duties of servanthood, and I fulfil yours by disclosing to you the mysteries of lordship. Or: fulfil My covenant by observing the forms of the Sacred Law, and I fulfil yours by guiding you to the beacon of the Path. Or: fulfil My covenant by travelling the Path, and I fulfil yours by bringing you to the very reality. Or: fulfil My covenant by immersion in the ocean of witnessing, and I fulfil yours through unceasing ascent towards the loving King. Direct fear and desire to Me alone, turning to Me in every request and need. I embrace you with My care and love and grant you immense beneficence and support. Believe in the gifts of My mysteries and blessings that I send down upon My friends’ hearts, confirming what I bestowed on My messengers and prophets. Everything that appears upon the friends of God is a miracle of the prophets and a confirmation of them. Do not hasten to deny My friends and so become the cause of driving My servants from My door. Do not let love of leadership and rank prevent your submission to My friends; do not watch for another besides Me, lest I withhold from you the witnessing of My mystery. Do not clothe truth in falsehood, displaying the marks of the righteous while concealing the character of transgressors, wearing the garb of God’s friends while acting as the misguided do. Once you recognize special election in one of My servants, do not hide it from the people of My love and affection. Establish the prayer of hearts by submission beneath the unfolding decrees; render the alms of souls through humility and brokenness. Be with the humble and bow with those who bow: I grant you My aid and victory and pour upon you from the ocean of My kindness and goodness. “I am with those whose hearts are broken for My sake.” [B039]"},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>The Real Most High then rebukes those among the People of the Book and others who know the truth but deprive themselves of it, saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real Most High then rebukes those among the People of the Book and others who know the truth but deprive themselves of it, saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[],"english_characters":5870,"arabic_characters":4292},{"id":"q2-44","q":"2:44","s":2,"surah":"Al-Baqara","title":"2:44 · Admonishing others while neglecting oneself","source":"Cairo print · Volume I, pp. 100–101","cairo":"I:100–101","source_page_first":100,"source_page_last":101,"ar":"أَتَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبِرِّ وَتَنْسَوْنَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ تَتْلُونَ الْكِتابَ أَفَلا تَعْقِلُونَ (44)\nقلت: البر، بالكسر: يجمع وجوه الخير وأنواع الطاعات، والنسيانُ: الترك.\nيقول الحق جلّ جلاله فى توبيخ أحبار اليهود، كانوا إذا استرشدهم أحد من العرب دلّوه على الإسلام، وقالوا له: دين محمد حق، وهم يمتنعون منه، وقيل: كانوا يأمرون الناس بالصدقة وهم يبخلون، فقال لهم: كيف تَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبِرِّ والإحسان، وتتركون أَنْفُسَكُمْ في الكفر والعصيان، وأنتم تدرسون التوراة الصحيح، وتعلمون أن ذلك من أقبح القبيح؟، أفلا عقل لكم يزجركم عن هذه الخصلة الذميمة؟ فإن من شأن العقل التمييز بين القبيح والحسن والنافع والضار، فكل من تقدم لما فيه ضرره فلا عقل له.\nالإشارة: كل مَن أشار إلى مقام لم يبلغْ قدمه إليه، فهذا التوبيخ متوجِّهُ إليه، وكل مَن ذكر غيره بعيب لم يتخلص منه، قيل له: أتأمر الناس بالبر وتنسى نفسك خالية منه، فلا يسلم من توبيخ هذه الآية من أهل التذكير إلا الفرد النادر من أهل الصفاء والوفاء.\nوقال البيضاوي: (المراد بها حثّ الواعظ على تزكية النفس، والإقبال عليها بالتكميل لتُقَوم فيُقَيِّم، لا منع الفاسق عن الوعظ، فإن الإخلال بأحد الأمرين المأمور بهما لا يوجب الإخلال بالآخر) . فانظره. وتأمل قول القائل:\nيا أيهَا الرجلُ المعلِّمُ غيرَه ... هلاَّ لنفسِك كانَ ذا التعليمُ\nتَصِف الدواءَ لِذي السقامِ وذي الضنَا ... ومِن الضَّنَا وجَواهُ أنتَ سقيمُ\nوأراكَ تلقحُ بالرشادِ عقُولَنا ... نُصْحاً، وأنت مِن الرشادِ عديمُ\nابدأ بنفسِك فانْهَهَا عَن غَيَّها ... فإذا انتهتْ عنه فأنتَ حكيمُ\nفَهُناك يُقْبَلُ إن وعظتَ، ويُقتدَى ... بالقول منكَ، وينفعُ التعليمُ\nلا تَنْهَ عن خُلقٍ وتأتيَ مثلَه ... عارٌ علَيكَ إذا فعلتَ عظيمُ\nلكن مَنْ حصل له بعض الصفاء، ذكر غيره ونفسه معهم، وكان بعض أشياخنا يقول حين يذكر الفقراء: نحن إنما ننبح على نفوسنا.\nثم أشار الحق تعالى إلى الدواء، فقال:","quran_ar":"أَتَأْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبِرِّ وَتَنْسَوْنَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ تَتْلُونَ الْكِتابَ أَفَلا تَعْقِلُونَ (44)","quran_en":"44. Do you enjoin righteousness upon people and forget yourselves, while you recite the Book? Will you not understand?","segments":[{"type":"language","title":"Righteousness and forgetting","html":"<p>I say: righteousness (<i>birr<\/i>, <bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">البر<\/bdi>), with kasra, embraces every form of goodness and kind of obedience. Forgetting (<bdi class=\"ar-term\" dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">النسيان<\/bdi>) means leaving aside.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"I say: righteousness ( birr , البر ), with kasra, embraces every form of goodness and kind of obedience. Forgetting ( النسيان ) means leaving aside."},{"type":"exposition","title":"A rebuke to those who know but do not act","html":"<p>The Real, glorious is His majesty, says in reproach to the Jewish learned men: when an Arab sought their direction, they directed him to Islam, saying that Muḥammad’s religion was true, while themselves abstaining from it. Alternatively, they commanded others to give charity but were themselves miserly. He says: how do you enjoin righteousness and beneficence upon people and leave yourselves in unbelief and disobedience, although you study the authentic Torah and know this to be among the ugliest acts? Have you no understanding to restrain you from this blameworthy quality? The rational intellect distinguishes ugly from beautiful and beneficial from harmful; one who deliberately approaches what harms him does not act with understanding.<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real, glorious is His majesty, says in reproach to the Jewish learned men: when an Arab sought their direction, they directed him to Islam, saying that Muḥammad’s religion was true, while themselves abstaining from it. Alternatively, they commanded others to give charity but were themselves miserly. He says: how do you enjoin righteousness and beneficence upon people and leave yourselves in unbelief and disobedience, although you study the authentic Torah and know this to be among the ugliest acts? Have you no understanding to restrain you from this blameworthy quality? The rational intellect distinguishes ugly from beautiful and beneficial from harmful; one who deliberately approaches what harms him does not act with understanding."},{"type":"spiritual","title":"The admonisher’s responsibility to his own soul","html":"<p>Whoever points towards a station his own foot has not reached is addressed by this rebuke. Whoever reminds another of a fault from which he has not freed himself is told: do you enjoin righteousness upon others and forget that your own soul is empty of it? Among those who give reminders, only the rare individual possessed of purity and fidelity escapes this verse’s reproach.<\/p><p>Al-Bayḍāwī says: “Its purpose is to urge the admonisher to purify his soul and turn to its perfection, so that it is set right and he can set others right—not to prevent a transgressor from admonishing. Neglecting one of two commanded duties does not necessitate neglecting the other.” Consider his words. Reflect also upon the poet’s saying:<\/p><blockquote class=\"poetry\">You who teach another,<br>why was this instruction not for yourself?<br>You prescribe medicine for the sick and wasted,<br>while you yourself are sick with wasting and its pain.<br>I see you implant guidance in our minds<br>as counsel, while yourself devoid of guidance.<br>Begin with yourself: restrain it from its error;<br>once it desists, you are indeed wise.<br>Then, when you admonish, it is accepted;<br>your words are followed, and instruction benefits.<br>Do not forbid a trait and then perform its like:<br>great is your shame if you do so.<\/blockquote><p>Yet one who possesses some purity may remind others and include himself among them. One of our shaykhs, when reminding the spiritual poor, used to say: “We are only barking at our own souls.”<\/p>","authorial":true,"text":"Whoever points towards a station his own foot has not reached is addressed by this rebuke. Whoever reminds another of a fault from which he has not freed himself is told: do you enjoin righteousness upon others and forget that your own soul is empty of it? Among those who give reminders, only the rare individual possessed of purity and fidelity escapes this verse’s reproach. Al-Bayḍāwī says: “Its purpose is to urge the admonisher to purify his soul and turn to its perfection, so that it is set right and he can set others right—not to prevent a transgressor from admonishing. Neglecting one of two commanded duties does not necessitate neglecting the other.” Consider his words. Reflect also upon the poet’s saying: You who teach another, why was this instruction not for yourself? You prescribe medicine for the sick and wasted, while you yourself are sick with wasting and its pain. I see you implant guidance in our minds as counsel, while yourself devoid of guidance. Begin with yourself: restrain it from its error; once it desists, you are indeed wise. Then, when you admonish, it is accepted; your words are followed, and instruction benefits. Do not forbid a trait and then perform its like: great is your shame if you do so. Yet one who possesses some purity may remind others and include himself among them. One of our shaykhs, when reminding the spiritual poor, used to say: “We are only barking at our own souls.”"},{"type":"transition","title":"","html":"<p>The Real Most High then points to the remedy, saying:<\/p>","authorial":false,"text":"The Real Most High then points to the remedy, saying:"}],"cairo_notes":[],"english_characters":2377,"arabic_characters":1675}];
